<p class=3D"kicker">bsv-wallet =C2=B7 implementation review</p>
<h1>Dead-End Fixes Review</h1>
<p class=3D"meta">31 commits, dfa97d0 =E2=86=92 4c1b3b1 =C2=B7 ~10,000 line=
s added =C2=B7 118 test suites green (1,378 tests, 8s) =C2=B7 14 review age=
nts, every claim adversarially re-verified</p>

<p>The implementation is <strong>substantially good work</strong>. The arch=
itecture the audit asked for is present and mostly right: the control chann=
el exists, NACK-before-ack ordering is correct, the delivering checkpoint c=
loses the crash window, environmental failures no longer burn retry attempt=
s, the background tasks exist, and the repair flow ships. Test coverage is =
real =E2=80=94 42 new or extended test files, and reviewers repeatedly foun=
d guards already in place where they expected bugs.</p>

<p>It is <strong>not ready to ship as-is.</strong> Two defects are severe e=
nough to make the wallet worse than before these commits, and both are in c=
ode that runs automatically. Neither is a design failure =E2=80=94 both are=
 a missing check in an otherwise sound mechanism.</p>

