<h2 id=3D"verdict">The verdict against the four criteria</h2>
<div class=3D"tablewrap">
<table>
<tbody><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Assessment</th></tr>
<tr><td>Robust</td><td><strong>Not yet.</strong> The mechanisms are right b=
ut three of them fail open in the dangerous direction: an unauthenticated c=
ontrol message destroys a payment token, a network outage marks good coins =
unspendable, and one poisoned row disables the whole repair pass.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stable</td><td><strong>Mostly.</strong> Tests are green and the cra=
sh windows the audit named are genuinely closed. Remaining instability is c=
oncentrated in shared-mutable-state races (the credit mutex, the consume-on=
ce header-miss slot, the cancel-vs-drain snapshot) rather than in the core =
flows.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fast</td><td><strong>Weakest dimension.</strong> Several new paths =
do unbounded work on the JS thread inside the 5-second monitor loop: a full=
 <code>outputs</code> table scan in an exclusive transaction, an O(N=C2=B2)=
 inbox relist, an unpruned pending queue parsed per screen refresh, and a r=
e-enabled audit task polling every minute.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Optimal</td><td><strong>Close, with two ordering mistakes.</strong>=
 Running the release spec-op before the change-recovery scan forfeits recov=
ery; the tested <code>reviewStatus</code> twin is not the code that runs in=
 production.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>

<h2 id=3D"blockers">The two blockers</h2>

<h3>1 =C2=B7 Anyone can delete someone else's pending payment</h3>
<div class=3D"callout warn">
<p><code>payment_cancelled</code> is acted on without checking who sent it.=
</p>
</div>
<p>The receiver's wallet polls the control box automatically on home-screen=
 focus and on opening the send screen. When a <code>payment_cancelled</code=
> arrives, <a href=3D"https://e6d89085-0be8-4e9e-b419-95aa3f6c0e82.frame.cl=
audeusercontent.com/_f/1788232741-4780/?__frame_t=3DpRsrpWGatgbqBIlyu0UR3Yp=
l.533ea1c7-e2ae-4058-a828-3cd9c10b30c3.9c29142a-7a07-4990-b7e7-5d21852ec6c2=
.1788236664&amp;__frame_v=3Dmanifest.aecc8e7118d82208.json#resend-cancel-no=
-sender-auth"><code>dropInboxTokenForTxid</code></a> lists the payment inbo=
x, matches tokens <em>by txid alone</em>, and acknowledges them =E2=80=94 a=
n irreversible server-side delete. The control message's authenticated <cod=
e>sender</code> is right there in the message and is never compared against=
 the token's sender.</p>
<p>A broadcast payment's txid is public on-chain. So any third party who wa=
tches the chain can send one forged message and permanently destroy the der=
ivation data a receiver needs to claim money that is already theirs =E2=80=
=94 precisely during the window (offline, headers behind, needs-attention) =
that this whole feature exists to protect. The good news: the messagebox la=
yer already authenticates <code>sender</code> via BRC-31 mutual auth, so th=
e fix is one comparison, plus the same treatment for the resend path's reci=
pient fallback. Tests only ever exercise a matching sender, which is why it=
 slipped through.</p>

<h3>2 =C2=B7 Check Wallet can zero a healthy balance</h3>
<div class=3D"callout warn">
<p>The repair flow releases outputs on <em>=E2=80=9Cnot confirmed unspent=
=E2=80=9D</em> rather than on <em>=E2=80=9Cconfirmed spent=E2=80=9D</em> =
=E2=80=94 and a network error looks like the former.</p>
</div>
<p>The coins step calls <code>listOutputs({ basket: specOpInvalidChange, ta=
gs: ['all','release'] })</code>. Inside the library, <code>Services.isUtxo<=
/code> returns <code>or.isUtxo =3D=3D=3D true</code> =E2=80=94 so when What=
sOnChain (the only registered provider) errors, times out, or rate-limits, =
<code>getUtxoStatus</code> returns <code>status:'error'</code> and <code>is=
Utxo()</code> returns <strong>false</strong>, not undefined. Every scanned =
output lands in the release set and is marked <code>spendable =3D 0</code>.=
</p>
<p>The screen auto-runs on mount with no online gate and no cancellation. T=
he same call runs after restore-from-backup. So a user who taps =E2=80=9CCh=
eck Wallet=E2=80=9D on a bad connection =E2=80=94 or restores their wallet =
on hotel wifi =E2=80=94 can watch their spendable balance go to zero, with =
no automatic path back. That is a worse dead end than the one the button wa=
s built to fix.</p>
<p>There is a second, network-independent version of the same bug: the scan=
 includes <code>nosend</code> and <code>unproven</code> transactions, so a =
queued offline payment's change output is never a UTXO yet, gets released, =
and stays unspendable forever after the payment posts =E2=80=94 the exact q=
ueued-offline case the plan's own guardrail said to skip.</p>

<h2 id=3D"themes">Recurring themes worth fixing as classes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Trusting the wire.</strong> Both criticals and four more find=
ings share one root: a value that arrives over the network (control-message=
 txid, WoC's inability to answer) is treated as authority for a destructive=
 local write. Every destructive path needs a positive confirmation, not an =
absence of contradiction.</li>
  <li><strong>Swallowing errors into =E2=80=9Cfine=E2=80=9D.</strong> All s=
ix ports in the Check flow catch everything and return zero counts, so a ru=
n in which nothing executed still ends on <em>=E2=80=9CEverything looks goo=
d=E2=80=9D</em> with a success haptic =E2=80=94 and the Retry button that e=
xists is unreachable. The same reflex hides the <code>reviewStatus</code> r=
ollback described below.</li>
  <li><strong>Tests that miss production.</strong> <code>reviewStatusSql.te=
st.ts</code> exercises <code>reviewStatusOnDb</code>, a raw-SQL twin nothin=
g in the app calls; the shipping implementation in <code>StorageExpoSQLite<=
/code> uses <code>updateTransactionStatus</code> instead =E2=80=94 which th=
rows on a completed transaction, rolling back all three repair rules inside=
 a single wrapping transaction. One proven-but-invalid-req row disables the=
 repair permanently, silently, every run.</li>
  <li><strong>Consume-once state read too early.</strong> <code>takeLastMis=
sHeight</code> is snapshotted <em>before</em> the credit pass runs and is s=
hared by three consumers, so a headers-behind failure is misclassified stru=
ctural on first occurrence and a joining caller can destroy the marker =E2=
=80=94 which means the wallet auto-NACKs payments that only needed header s=
ync. This defeats the environmental classification for its single most impo=
rtant case.</li>
  <li><strong>Unbounded work on the JS thread.</strong> <code>reviewStatus<=
/code> full-scans <code>outputs</code> with no <code>WHERE</code> inside an=
 exclusive write transaction, on tables that can never be purged; <code>acc=
eptWithRetry</code> relists the whole inbox per failing payment (O(N=C2=B2)=
); the localpay pending queue never prunes and is re-parsed with full BEEF =
blobs on every home-screen refresh; the re-enabled <code>ReviewProvenTxs</c=
ode> polls every minute with two HTTP calls per pass.</li>
  <li><strong>New always-on paths with no notification.</strong> <code>Task=
CreditInbox</code> credits payments in the background but raises no toast, =
sound, or overlay =E2=80=94 the money lands silently. The nearby and addres=
s rails already have exactly this notification hook wired.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id=3D"good">What's genuinely good</h2>
<p>Worth stating plainly, because the reviewers went looking for these and =
found them already handled:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>NACK-before-ack holds on every discard path.</strong> A faile=
d control send leaves the inbox row in place rather than deleting the deriv=
ation data.</li>
  <li><strong>Auto-NACK fires once, not per poll</strong> =E2=80=94 attempt=
 state is persisted in KV and shared between the screen and the monitor tas=
k.</li>
  <li><strong>The automatic poll path is read-only.</strong> Listing resend=
 requests never rebuilds, refetches, or redelivers; every WoC-fetching path=
 is behind an explicit user tap.</li>
  <li><strong>The delivering checkpoint is correct</strong>, and cancel now=
 returns <code>needsAbandon</code> instead of aborting a transaction the re=
cipient may hold.</li>
  <li><strong><code>broadcastNoSend</code> matches the real SDK contract</s=
trong> =E2=80=94 <code>'unproven' | 'sending' | 'failed'</code> =E2=80=94 a=
nd an aborted request does surface as <code>failed</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>The mint-leak abort is properly guarded:</strong> its own fai=
lure only warns, and the original save error is rethrown.</li>
  <li><strong>Quarantine beats the old behavior:</strong> a corrupt pending=
 blob now refuses to read as empty, so a later write can no longer destroy =
queued payments.</li>
  <li><strong>Nearby frame persistence happens before any broadcast</strong=
>, online or off =E2=80=94 the exact ordering the audit demanded.</li>
  <li><strong>i18n is complete</strong> =E2=80=94 every new key defined acr=
oss all 12 locales; no raw-key renders found.</li>
  <li><strong>Poll discipline on the receive screen</strong> is focus-gated=
, AppState-gated, single-flight, and torn down on unmount.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id=3D"order">What to fix, in order</h2>
<div class=3D"tablewrap">
<table>
<tbody><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Fix</th></tr>
<tr><td>Blocker</td><td>Require <code>m.sender =3D=3D=3D controlMsg.sender<=
/code> before acking any inbox token on <code>payment_cancelled</code>; nev=
er fall back to the requester as resend recipient (record the recipient pub=
key as an action label at send time). Add mismatched-sender tests.</td></tr=
>
<tr><td>Blocker</td><td>Never release on an inconclusive answer: call <code=
>getUtxoStatus</code> and release only on <code>status =3D=3D=3D 'success' =
&amp;&amp; isUtxo =3D=3D=3D false</code>. Gate both call sites on <code>get=
Online()</code>, and exclude txids with live <code>offline_actions</code> r=
ows and <code>nosend</code>/<code>unproven</code> transactions.</td></tr>
<tr><td>High</td><td>Add <code>AND t.provenTxId IS NULL AND t.status &lt;&g=
t; 'completed'</code> to the invalid-req query, wrap each per-tx status wri=
te in try/catch, and point the tests at the code that actually ships.</td><=
/tr>
<tr><td>High</td><td>Make the header-miss signal non-consuming and read it =
inside <code>classify</code> at failure time, after the join check =E2=80=
=94 otherwise the environmental classification does not work for its main c=
ase.</td></tr>
<tr><td>High</td><td>Report per-step outcomes from the Check flow (<code>ok=
</code>/<code>error</code>) so =E2=80=9Ccouldn't check=E2=80=9D is distingu=
ishable from =E2=80=9Cnothing wrong=E2=80=9D, and the Retry button becomes =
reachable.</td></tr>
<tr><td>High</td><td>Re-read the outbox entry from storage inside <code>can=
celOutboxPayment</code> before aborting; broaden the environmental regex (d=
atabase-locked, =E2=80=9Cfailed to retrieve messages=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9Cnot=
 found on refresh=E2=80=9D); repair <code>PENDING_KEY</code> after quaranti=
ne and prune completed entries.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Performance pass: bound <code>reviewStatus</code>'s =
scans with a <code>WHERE</code> and move them out of the exclusive transact=
ion; cap the inbox relist; restore <code>ReviewProvenTxs</code> to a sane c=
adence with an offline gate; prune sent outbox entries from the background,=
 not only on the Pay screen.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Medium</td><td>Raise the arrival notification from <code>TaskCredit=
Inbox</code> using the hook the nearby and sweep paths already use.</td></t=
r>
