<p>None of this is rework. The blockers are a comparison and a status check=
; the highs are a WHERE clause, a moved read, and an error field.</p>

<h2 id=3D"findings">All findings</h2>
<p>69 claims, each re-verified by an independent adversarial reviewer again=
st the diff; 68 survived. Grouped by area, criticals expanded, verifier cor=
rections shown where they narrow or sharpen the claim.</p>
<h3 class=3D"group-title" id=3D"g-resend">Resend loop &amp; control channel=
<span class=3D"group-count">8</span></h3>
<details class=3D"finding sev-critical" open=3D"" id=3D"resend-cancel-no-se=
nder-auth">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-critical">critical</span><span class=3D"f=
title">Forged payment_cancelled from any third party silently drops a victi=
m's uncredited payment token</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirm=
ed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A sends a p=
ayment to B (txid T); A broadcasts it, so T is public on-chain. B has not y=
et credited it (device offline, headers behind, or it is sitting as a needs=
-attention row). Attacker M =E2=80=94 who is neither A nor B and only needs=
 to know T =E2=80=94 sends `{type:'payment_cancelled', txid:T}` to B's `pay=
ment_control` box. On B's next automatic Home/HandleSend poll, `listPending=
ResendRequests` -&gt; `consumePaymentCancelled` -&gt; `dropInboxTokenForTxi=
d` lists B's `payment_inbox`, matches the token purely by `txidFromInboxBod=
y(m.body) =3D=3D=3D txid`, and calls `acknowledgeMessage` on it.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>`dropInboxTokenF=
orTxid` (handleResendRequests.ts:67-77) and `consumePaymentCancelled` (80-9=
2) match and delete inbox tokens by txid ONLY. The `payment_cancelled` cont=
rol message's authenticated `msg.sender` is available but is never compared=
 against the inbox token's `sender`. `acknowledgeMessage` is an irreversibl=
e server-side delete, so the derivation prefix/suffix B needs to internaliz=
e are destroyed. The docstring claim 'Already-internalized txs are left alo=
ne' is true only for already-acked tokens; it gives no protection to the un=
credited tokens this whole mechanism exists to protect. The path is fully a=
utomatic on B's side (WalletHomeScreen `pollResendRequests` on mount/focus,=
 HandleSend `pollResendRequests` on mount) =E2=80=94 no user action needed.=
 Tests (handleResendRequests.test.ts:229-281) only ever use a matching send=
er, so the gap is untested.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>An unauthorized thir=
d party who knows a public txid can permanently delete a real, delivered-bu=
t-uncredited payment from the receiver's inbox during the exact window the =
dead-end fixes target. The on-chain output still belongs to the receiver cr=
yptographically, but the derivation data is gone and there is no receiver-i=
nitiated resend, so the payment becomes uncreditable =E2=80=94 reintroducin=
g a payment dead end via an authorization gap.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Authentic=
ate the cancel: pass the control message's `msg.sender` into `dropInboxToke=
nForTxid` and only ack inbox messages where `m.sender =3D=3D=3D cancelSende=
r &amp;&amp; txidFromInboxBody(m.body) =3D=3D=3D txid`. A payment can only =
be cancelled by the party that sent it. Add a test with a mismatched sender=
 asserting the token is NOT dropped.</p>
