<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"resend-misdeliver-to-attacker">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">resend_request re-delivers a rebuilt token to the unauthenticated reques=
ter when the outbox entry is gone</span><span class=3D"vtag v-unverified">N=
ot re-verified</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A paid B (t=
xid T). A's outbox entry for T has been pruned (past 30-day SENT_RETENTION,=
 or dismissed) but the peerpay action is still within A's most-recent 1000 =
listActions. Attacker M sends `{type:'resend_request', txid:T, reason:'uncr=
editible'}` to A's `payment_control` box. A taps 'Resend'. `rebuildAndDeliv=
er` finds no outbox entry, so `recipient =3D entry?.recipient || recipientF=
romLabels(listed?.labels) || args.recipient`. peerpay actions carry only `l=
abels:['peerpay']` (no pubkey label), so `recipientFromLabels` is always un=
defined here, and `args.recipient` is `msg.sender` =3D M. A rebuilds the to=
ken (WoC refetch) and sendMessages it to M, then acks the request.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>handleResendRequ=
ests.ts:232-234 lets the wire `sender` become the delivery target whenever =
no outbox entry exists, with no check that the requester is the payment's a=
ctual recipient. `recipientFromLabels` (94-96) can never succeed for peerpa=
y actions because they are labelled only 'peerpay', so the attacker-control=
led `args.recipient` is the effective fallback.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>An attacker can caus=
e the sender to deliver a payment token (AtomicBEEF + derivation nonces) to=
 an arbitrary identity. Funds cannot be stolen =E2=80=94 the output is lock=
ed to a key derived toward the real recipient B, so M cannot internalize =
=E2=80=94 but it is unauthorized disclosure/misdelivery, it consumes a WoC =
fetch, and it consumes (acks) the request so the legitimate recipient's dea=
d end is not fixed. When the outbox entry still exists, `entry.recipient` c=
orrectly wins, so the window is limited to pruned/dismissed entries.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>When the =
delivery target is derived only from the wire `sender` (no outbox entry, no=
 verifiable recipient), do not treat `msg.sender` as authoritative. Persist=
 the recipient identity with the sent action (e.g. a pubkey label or a reta=
ined sender-side record beyond 30 days) and require the resend target to ma=
tch it; otherwise refuse the resend rather than trusting the requester.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/handle=
ResendRequests.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"resend-unbounded-pending-spam">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Unknown-txid resend_request spam accumulates forever, poisons the persis=
ted banner, and can never be cleared</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed"=
>Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Attacker fl=
oods A's `payment_control` box with `resend_request`s for random/unknown tx=
ids. On every Home poll, `listPendingResendRequests` pushes every one into =
`pending` (no validation that the txid is a payment A actually sent, no ded=
up) and `storeUnansweredResends` rewrites the whole array to KV. The Home '=
Resend requested' banner shows because `pendingResends.length &gt; 0`. When=
 A taps Resend, `handleResendRequests` cannot rebuild any of them (no outbo=
x/action match), so they are re-added to `pending`, never acked, and re-per=
sisted.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>listPendingResen=
dRequests (177-202) and handleResendRequests (263-297) neither validate tha=
t a resend_request corresponds to a known outbound payment nor bound the nu=
mber retained, and unfulfillable requests are never acknowledged so they re=
main in the box permanently. `storeUnansweredResends` serialises the entire=
 attacker-controlled list every poll.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Persistent griefing:=
 an attacker can make the home-screen resend banner appear permanently and =
un-clearable, bloat the `peerpay_unanswered_resends` KV blob, and force per=
-message work on every poll/tap. Defeats the feature it supports.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Before pe=
rsisting/showing a resend_request, confirm the txid matches an outbox entry=
 or a listActions peerpay action owned by this wallet; drop (ack) or ignore=
 requests that match nothing, and cap the retained/persisted list.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Bound and dedup the pending list, and acknowledge (drop) resend_req=
uests that reference no known outbound payment so unfulfillable spam cannot=
 accumulate or persist the banner.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/handle=
ResendRequests.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"resend-woc-amplification">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">handleResendRequests has no per-txid dedup, so duplicate requests multip=
ly WoC fetches and redeliveries</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Conf=
irmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The box hol=
ds N resend_requests for the same real txid T (attacker spam, or repeated N=
ACKs from the receiver). A taps Resend. handleResendRequests iterates all N=
 messages; for each it finds the outbox entry, calls `rebuildPeerPayToken` =
-&gt; `refetch(T)` (a WhatsOnChain HTTP GET) and a `sendMessage` redelivery=
, then acks.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The loop at hand=
leResendRequests.ts:263-293 processes every message independently with no d=
edup by txid and no memoisation of `refetch`. `makeBeefRepair` hits WoC per=
 call (beefRepair.ts:49). N duplicate requests =3D&gt; N network fetches + =
N redeliveries on the mobile JS thread.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Request amplificatio=
n / DoS: an attacker (or a noisy receiver) turns one real payment into N Wo=
C fetches and N inbox messages at the recipient. Runs on the UI thread and =
can stall it.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Deduplica=
te resend_requests by txid before rebuilding (process each txid at most onc=
e per pass), and/or memoise refetch per txid within a pass.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Dedup requests by txid before rebuild, and memoize refetch per txid=
 within a single handleResendRequests run.</p>
