ResendRequests.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"resend-duplicate-token-rows">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">Reb=
uilt token uses fresh BEEF -&gt; new HMAC messageId -&gt; duplicate inbox r=
ows; original uncreditable token is never cleared</span><span class=3D"vtag=
 v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>B's token f=
or T failed to credit and stays in B's inbox as a needs-attention row (neve=
r acked). B's app NACKs; A taps Resend. rebuildToken refetches a FRESH Atom=
icBEEF from WoC (rebuildToken.ts:42), so the delivered body differs from th=
e original. messageId is HMAC(JSON.stringify(body)) (MessageBoxClient gener=
ateMessageId), so the rebuilt token gets a NEW messageId and lands as a sec=
ond inbox message for the same txid.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Re-delivery is n=
ot idempotent at the messagebox layer whenever the BEEF bytes change (which=
 is the whole point of rebuilding after a reorg). The original failed messa=
ge is never acknowledged, so B now has two rows for one payment. If the fre=
sh one credits, the stale one keeps failing ('already internalized' -&gt; s=
tructural) and remains a permanent needs-attention row, inflating attention=
Count. The outbox.ts comment 'HMAC message id is idempotent' holds only for=
 `retryDelivery` (same stored bytes), not for the rebuild path.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Duplicate/phantom in=
box rows and an inflated attention badge that the user must manually Discar=
d; every extra resend adds another stuck row. Not fund loss, but a UX dead-=
end-adjacent artifact.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>When a re=
send for a txid is delivered, ack/replace any existing inbox messages and a=
ttempt-map entries for that same txid; or key inbox attempt/attention state=
 by txid rather than messageId so a re-delivery supersedes the prior copy.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>On a successful rebuilt-token credit, reconcile/ack any other inbox=
 rows sharing the same txid; or have the sender ack/replace rather than app=
end when re-delivering.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/rebuil=
dToken.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/handleResen=
dRequests.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"resend-kv-unbounded-growth">
