<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"resend-listactions-cap-and-labels"=
>
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">lis=
tPeerPayAction 1000-limit and peerpay-only labels break legitimate resends =
of older payments</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></=
summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A legitimat=
ely sent a payment more than 1000 peerpay-actions ago, the outbox entry has=
 been pruned (&gt;30 days), and B asks for a resend. `makeListPeerPayAction=
` calls listActions with `limit:1000` and no offset/pagination, so T is not=
 in the cache; rebuild returns undefined and the resend fails with a generi=
c error.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>makeListPeerPayA=
ction (121-148) caps at 1000 with no pagination, and recipientFromLabels (9=
4-96) can never resolve for peerpay actions (labelled only 'peerpay'), so a=
n older payment cannot be rebuilt or addressed once its outbox entry is gon=
e.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Legitimate resends o=
f older payments silently fail; combined with resend-misdeliver-to-attacker=
