card of an unparseable token sends a resend_request the sender can never fu=
lfil</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>B discards =
an unparseable inbox token. `discardIncoming` (handle.ts:335-346) has no at=
omic txid, so it puts `String(payment.messageId)` in the `txid` field (and =
also a `messageId` field). A receives this resend_request; handleResendRequ=
ests keys lookup on `parsed.txid` only, which is a messageId, matching no o=
utbox entry or action -&gt; undefined -&gt; pending, never acked.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The resend_reque=
st carries a real `messageId` field, but handleResendRequests (rebuildAndDe=
liver at 220-234) ignores `parsed.messageId` and only uses `parsed.txid`. S=
o a messageId-as-txid request is permanently unresolvable and un-ackable, a=
ccumulating like the spam case.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>NACKs for unparseabl=
e tokens produce permanent un-clearable pending entries on the sender and c=
