<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"inbox-cancel-vs-drain-race">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">T=
askDrainOutbox background delivery races the Cancel flow's stale delivered/=
delivering snapshot</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span>=
</summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>An unsent o=
utbox entry exists (delivery failed earlier). The user opens HandleSend and=
 taps Cancel; while the confirmation alert is open (an unbounded human-scal=
e window), TaskDrainOutbox fires (it retries every 10s-5min whenever unsent=
 entries exist and the device is online, WalletContext.tsx:1298-1320), runs=
 retryDelivery (handle.ts:589-599): sets delivering:true, sendMessage deliv=
ers the token, sets delivered:true, broadcasts. The user then confirms Canc=
el.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>cancelOutboxPaym=
ent (handle.ts:536-537) guards only on the `entry` object the UI captured w=
hen the row rendered (HandleSend.tsx:349-351, 401-407) =E2=80=94 it never r=
e-reads the entry from storage. With the stale snapshot (delivered/deliveri=
ng undefined) the 'undelivered' path passes the guard, calls abortPeerPayNo=
send (handle.ts:549-556, which swallows abort errors) and removeOutboxEntry=
. Two interleavings: (a) drain's sendMessage lands before/while the abort s=
ucceeds =E2=86=92 the recipient holds a token for a transaction whose input=
s the sender just freed =E2=80=94 the recipient's wallet internalizes an un=
proven tx that will never confirm and receives no payment_cancelled notice =
(the 'undelivered' path sends none); (b) drain broadcast already succeeded =
=E2=86=92 abortAction throws, is swallowed, the entry is removed and the se=
nder is told the payment was cancelled although the money actually went out=
. Before this change retry was manual-only from the same screen (serialized=
 by retryingId); the background task is what makes the guard's snapshot sta=
leness exploitable.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Recipient shown mone=
y that never arrives (a new payment dead end of exactly the class the fixes=
 target), or sender believing a completed payment was cancelled. No fund th=
eft, but fund-state confusion on both sides with no corrective message sent=
.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Inside ca=
ncelOutboxPayment, re-read the entry by id from storage and re-check delive=
red/delivering immediately before aborting; add a module-level per-entry in=
-flight set shared by retryDelivery and cancelOutboxPayment (the same patte=
rn creditInbox.ts uses for the inbox) so a cancel waits for or is refused d=
uring an active delivery, and vice versa.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>One precondition is overstated: 'delivery failed earlier' does NOT =
leave delivered/delivering undefined in the new code =E2=80=94 sendViaHandl=
e persists delivering:true BEFORE sendMessage (handle.ts:490-495), so a fai=
led delivery routes the UI to the abandon sheet, not the undelivered path. =
The undelivered-path race needs a pre-upgrade legacy entry (delivering chec=
kpoint added in e8d22c7), a crash between saveOutboxEntry and the checkpoin=
t, or a failed checkpoint write (handle.ts:502-509 leaves delivering unset)=
. The same stale-snapshot race also hits the mainline abandon path: while t=
he sheet is open, drain can deliver+broadcast; abandon then sends payment_c=
ancelled (recipient acks away the token via dropInboxTokenForTxid, handleRe=
sendRequests.ts:67-77) for money that actually left the sender =E2=80=94 a =
comparable dead end.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/rails/hand=
le.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/HandleSend=
.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/context/WalletContext.ts=
x</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"inbox-lastmiss-slot-consumed-by-j=
oining-callers">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">S=
ingle consumable lastMissHeight slot is snapshotted pre-pass and clobbered =
across three consumers</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</sp=
an></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Headers are=
 behind, so BEEF verify fails with 'The tx parameter must be valid AtomicBE=
EF' and OfflineFirstChaintracks sets lastMissHeight DURING the pass (Offlin=
eFirstChaintracks.ts:73,84,112). The monitor task (WalletContext.tsx:1279-1=
282) and the HandleReceive 5s poll (HandleReceive.tsx:494-497) each call ma=
keCreditClassifier, which consumes takeLastMissHeight at pass START (credit=
Errors.ts:38). When one caller's creditInboxOnce JOINS the other's in-fligh=
t pass (creditInbox.ts:193), its freshly-built classifier =E2=80=94 holding=
 the consumed miss =E2=80=94 is discarded.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Two coupled flaw=
s: (a) the snapshot is taken before the pass, so the pass in which a miss f=
irst occurs always classifies it structural (the miss only becomes visible =
to the NEXT pass) =E2=80=94 one attempt of two is burned deterministically =
for every headers-behind payment; (b) because the slot is consume-once and =
shared by the monitor task, the receive-screen poll, and WalletCheckScreen =
(WalletCheckScreen.tsx:190), a consumer that then joins an in-flight pass d=
estroys the miss marker without using it, so the next real pass classifies =
the same headers-behind failure structural again =E2=80=94 attempts reach 2=
 and the wallet NACKs a payment that only needed header sync. The 5s screen=
 poll interleaving with the 10s+ task backoff makes the join-and-discard or=
dering routine while the user watches the receive screen.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Valid payments stuck=
 behind header sync get auto-NACKed ('uncreditible') or stop being retried,=
 defeating the environmental classification for its primary case (the 'vali=
d AtomicBEEF' missing-root error that matches no regex).</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Make last=
MissHeight non-consuming (peek + timestamp, cleared on successful verify) o=
r per-pass: re-read it inside classify at failure time rather than snapshot=
ting before the pass; only creditInboxOnce's actually-running pass should c=
onsume it (e.g. pass takeLastMissHeight into runCreditInbox and build the c=
lassifier there, after the join check).</p>

