<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"inbox-structural-misclassificatio=
n-nacks-valid-payments">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">E=
nvironmental failures classified structural burn both attempts and auto-NAC=
K healthy payments</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span><=
/summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A creditabl=
e payment fails while the device reports online: (1) acceptWithRetry's re-l=
ist throws 'Failed to retrieve messages from any host' (MessageBoxClient li=
stMessages when the box flakes mid-pass) =E2=80=94 that message replaces th=
e original error; (2) AuthFetch throws 'Network error while sending authent=
icated request to &lt;host&gt;/.well-known/auth'; (3) the local SQLite data=
base is momentarily locked/closed (e.g. during a wallet rebuild) and intern=
alizeAction throws a storage error; (4) acceptWithRetry finds the message g=
one after a concurrent pass acked it and throws 'Payment not found on refre=
sh' (handle.ts:220). Two such passes occur.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>classifyCreditEr=
ror's environmental regex (creditErrors.ts:22) matches only /network reques=
t failed|timed? ?out|chaintracks/i. None of the four messages above match, =
so all are classified 'structural', increment attempts (handle.ts:301-303),=
 and at MAX_AUTO_ATTEMPTS=3D2 fire onGiveUp which sends a resend_request NA=
CK 'uncreditible' to the sender (creditInbox.ts:150-161) for a payment the =
wallet could still credit. Notably the MAX_AUTO_ATTEMPTS doc itself (handle=
.ts:244-247) names 'offline, a locked database, a stale token' as the commo=
n transient failures, yet a locked-database error is classified structural.=
 The sibling helper isMessageBoxNetworkError (handle.ts:570-573) already kn=
ows the 'network error' shape but classifyCreditError does not reuse it.</p=
>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>The auto-NACK tells =
the sender their payment was uncreditable and stops auto-retry on the recip=
