<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"inbox-acceptpayments-default-tr=
ue-inline-internalize">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Every credit pass calls listIncomingPayments with acceptPayments default=
ing to true =E2=80=94 attacker-triggerable inline internalizeAction</span><=
span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Anyone can =
post to any payment_inbox. An attacker sends a body shaped as {message: ...=
, payment: {tx, outputs: [{protocol:'wallet payment',...}]}}. MessageBoxCli=
ent.parseMessageEnvelope lifts `payment` from the sender-controlled body (M=
essageBoxClient.ts:1108-1120); listMessages defaults acceptPayments to true=
 (MessageBoxClient.ts:1581-1583) and calls walletClient.internalizeAction o=
n it inline (MessageBoxClient.ts:1646-1652), with errors swallowed. PeerPay=
Client.listIncomingPayments passes no acceptPayments (PeerPayClient.ts:468-=
470), and creditInbox calls it at creditInbox.ts:123 =E2=80=94 from the bac=
kground monitor task (WalletContext.tsx:1283), the 5s screen poll, the acce=
ptWithRetry re-list (handle.ts:218), and WalletCheckScreen.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The new code dem=
onstrably knows about this hazard =E2=80=94 listRawInbox passes acceptPayme=
nts:false with the comment 'avoids fee auto-internalize' (creditInbox.ts:88=
-92) and listControlMessages does the same (control.ts:68-81) =E2=80=94 but=
 the primary listing in every credit pass leaves it enabled. Since the inne=
r wrapped message is not a valid token, such a message is never accepted/ac=
ked by the credit flow, so its envelope 'payment' is re-internalized (full =
SPV verify + storage attempt) on EVERY pass, forever, driven by the backgro=
und task even when no screen is open.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Attacker-reachable r=
epeated CPU (BEEF verify on the JS thread) and storage work in every monito=
r pass and screen poll; unaudited internalize side effects outside the atte=
mpts/NACK policy the new code builds. Also inconsistent with the design tha=
t all crediting flows through autoAcceptInbox.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Stop usin=
g PeerPayClient.listIncomingPayments in creditInbox: build the parsed list =
from the already-fetched raw listMessages({acceptPayments:false}) result vi=
a isPaymentTokenShape (all the pieces already exist in runCreditInbox), or =
upstream a listIncomingPayments option that forwards acceptPayments:false.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Minor cite fix: the 'avoids fee auto-internalize' comment lives at =
control.ts:68, not creditInbox.ts:88-92 (that site has the acceptPayments:f=
alse line without the comment). Internalize concurrency in the library is 2=
, decrypt is 4 (MessageBoxClient.ts:1648, 1654).</p>
