<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"inbox-drain-head-of-line-blocki=
ng">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">TaskDrainOutbox stops at the first throw with one shared backoff =E2=80=
=94 a permanently failing entry starves all later payments forever</span><s=
pan class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Entry A (ol=
dest unsent) fails structurally on every retry =E2=80=94 recipient has bloc=
ked the sender (server returns 'blocked' from the quote/send), the recipien=
t key is invalid, or the entry's stored messageBoxUrl is a dead host. Entri=
es B and C queued after it are deliverable.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>drainUnsentEntri=
es retries in creation order and the first throw aborts the rest (TaskDrain=
Outbox.ts:25-35); runTask's catch schedules the shared backoff (TaskDrainOu=
tbox.ts:97-101,115-118). There is no per-entry error state, no skip-after-N=
-failures, and no reordering, so B and C are never auto-retried while A exi=
sts, and the task re-hits the same dead entry every 5 minutes forever (hasP=
ending never clears). The design comment justifies stop-on-first-throw for =
'a down message box', but a per-entry failure hits the same wall on every b=
ackoff. The `stopped`/`remaining` fields are dead code =E2=80=94 remaining =
is always 0 when no throw occurs.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Payments behind a po=
isoned head entry silently never deliver in the background (manual per-row =
retry still works, but the whole point of the task was removing that depend=
ence); perpetual 5-minute retry churn against a permanent failure.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Catch per=
 entry, record consecutive failures on the entry (lastError already exists)=
, continue with the remaining entries, and skip entries whose recent failur=
e looks structural (reuse isMessageBoxNetworkError to distinguish); only st=
op the pass early on a network-shaped error.</p>

