ainOutbox.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/context/WalletCo=
ntext.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"inbox-flood-quadratic-relist-bl=
ocks-monitor">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">acceptWithRetry relists the whole box per failing payment: O(N=C2=B2) wo=
rk per pass and a fully blocked monitor loop</span><span class=3D"vtag v-co=
nfirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>An attacker=
 (or a burst of genuinely broken senders) puts N valid-shape tokens with ga=
rbage transactions in the box. Each pass, autoAcceptInbox attempts each one=
 sequentially; every failure makes acceptWithRetry call client.listIncoming=
Payments again (handle.ts:217-222), which re-fetches and re-decrypts (ECDH =
per message, mapWithConcurrency 4) the entire box =E2=80=94 N relists =C3=
=97 N decrypts, plus the envelope-internalize work from acceptpayments-defa=
ult-true, then a second internalize attempt per payment. Monitor.runOnce aw=
aits each task's runTask sequentially with no timeout, so TaskSendWaiting, =
TaskSendOffline, TaskNewHeader etc. all wait behind the pass.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Per-pass cost is=
 quadratic in inbox size and runs on the app JS thread inside the monitor l=
oop. The attempts ceiling bounds this to ~2 passes per junk message (good),=
 but a single flood makes the first passes take minutes, freezing backgroun=
d broadcasting and delaying offline drains; each junk row also becomes a pe=
rmanent needs-attention row the user must discard one by one, and each earn=
s the attacker a NACK response.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Cheap remote degrada=
tion of the wallet's background machinery and UI responsiveness; delayed re=
al payment broadcasts while the pass runs.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Reuse the=
 pass's initial listing for the retry lookup instead of relisting per payme=
nt (or relist at most once per pass); consider a per-pass cap on attempted =
payments and a size cap on attention rows from a single sender.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Two refinements: bad-shape/damaged junk is excluded from creditable=
 (creditInbox.ts:143) so it triggers no relist and no auto-NACK (only user-=
tap discard NACKs it) =E2=80=94 the quadratic cost needs valid-token-shape =
junk with garbage transactions; and if the flood is classified environmenta=
l (e.g. device flapping offline), attempts never count and the re-attempt w=
ork recurs beyond 2 passes.</p>
