<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>User taps R=
etry on an attention row while the message box is unreachable; runCredit's =
listIncomingPayments throws (fetchPayments' catch does not cover this path =
=E2=80=94 handleRetry calls runCredit directly).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>handleRetry (Han=
dleReceive.tsx:588-600) wraps runCredit in try/finally with no catch: the s=
pinner stops, no toast or state change occurs, and the rejection escapes to=
 an unhandled-promise warning. The user cannot distinguish 'retried and sti=
ll broken' from 'the retry never ran'.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A user explicitly ac=
ting on a stuck payment gets silence =E2=80=94 a minor but on-theme dead en=
d for the non-technical user these fixes target.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Add a cat=
ch that toasts via the same isMessageBoxNetworkError/userFacingPayError map=
ping fetchPayments uses for non-silent reads.</p>

