<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"inbox-per-tick-client-construction=
">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">New=
 PeerPayClient per pass/per entry redoes the auth handshake instead of reus=
ing a session</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summ=
ary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Every TaskC=
reditInbox pass builds a fresh PeerPayClient (WalletContext.tsx:1266-1274) =
and TaskDrainOutbox builds one per outbox ENTRY per pass (WalletContext.tsx=
:1303-1308).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Each new client =
carries an empty AuthFetch session, so every pass (and every drained entry)=
 re-runs the BRC-104 mutual-auth handshake and getPublicKey init round-trip=
s that a cached client (like HandleReceive's useMemo client) amortizes. Cor=
rectness is unaffected; this is pure per-tick network overhead on a task th=
at can run every 10 seconds.</p>
