<h3 class=3D"group-title" id=3D"g-send">Outbound send hardening<span class=
=3D"group-count">6</span></h3>
<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"send-payment-cancelled-unauthenti=
cated-token-drop">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">p=
ayment_cancelled is unauthenticated =E2=80=94 anyone can make a recipient d=
iscard an uncredited inbound payment</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed"=
>Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>An attacker=
 sends {type:'payment_cancelled', txid:&lt;a real inbound txid&gt;} to a vi=
ctim's payment_control box (anyone can post to any box). On the victim's ne=
xt home-screen focus, pollResendRequests -&gt; listPendingResendRequests (h=
andleResendRequests.ts:185-192) runs consumePaymentCancelled (79-92) -&gt; =
dropInboxTokenForTxid (67-77), which lists payment_inbox and acknowledges (=
deletes) every message whose token BEEF hashes to that txid. The original p=
ayment sender's identity (msg.sender on both the control message and the in=
box message) is never compared.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>consumePaymentCa=
ncelled/dropInboxTokenForTxid delete a still-uncredited inbound payment tok=
en purely on a txid match, with zero authentication that the payment_cancel=
led came from the party who originally sent the payment. The txid of a broa=
dcast payment is public on-chain, so it is guessable/observable. Deleting t=
he inbox token destroys the derivationPrefix/derivationSuffix the recipient=
 needs to internalize the on-chain output =E2=80=94 and it is deleted silen=
tly, without a NACK/resend_request, so no auto-recovery is triggered.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Griefing / fund-avai=
lability attack: a recipient who is briefly unable to credit a payment (off=
line, environmental chaintracks miss, needsAttention) can have that payment=
's derivation data deleted by a third party, leaving satoshis locked to the=
ir address on-chain that they can no longer spend without begging the sende=
r to resend. Directly contradicts the 'never a payment dead end' goal =E2=
=80=94 the attacker manufactures the dead end.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>In dropIn=
boxTokenForTxid, only ack an inbox message whose authenticated sender equal=
s the payment_cancelled control-message sender (m.sender =3D=3D=3D controlM=
sg.sender). Thread the control message's sender into consumePaymentCancelle=
d and compare per message before acking.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/handle=
ResendRequests.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/Walle=
tHomeScreen.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/=
HandleSend.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"send-credit-ack-batch-poison">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">acknowledgeCredited batches all pending acks; one stale id can strand ev=
ery later credited payment unacked</span><span class=3D"vtag v-partial">Par=
tially confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Payment A i=
s internalized but its acknowledgeMessage fails (offline), so A's id stays =
in the process-global pendingCreditAcks set (handle.ts:169,183). Later paym=
ent B is internalized; acknowledgeCredited acks [A,B] (184-187). If the box=
 has since dropped/expired A and returns an error for that id, and the serv=
er fails the whole batch, neither id is cleared =E2=80=94 B is credited but=
 never acked.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>pendingCreditAck=
s is a single global batch: success clears all, failure clears none. A perm=
anently-unackable id poisons the batch, so every subsequently credited paym=
ent is acked in the same doomed batch and never removed from the recipient'=
s box. Each poll then re-lists and re-internalizes those already-owned paym=
ents (internalizeAction is idempotent for owned outputs, so it silently no-=
ops) and re-fails the ack =E2=80=94 a wallet read/write per payment per ~5s=
 poll forever.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A stuck ack silently=
 degrades into perpetual re-credit churn: repeated listIncomingPayments + i=
nternalizeAction DB work every poll for payments that will never leave the =
box, on the mobile JS thread. No user-visible error, just battery/latency d=
rain and a box that never drains.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Ack ids i=
ndividually (or best-effort per id, removing only the ids the server confir=
med) instead of one all-or-nothing batch, so one unackable id cannot block =
the rest. Bound/evict entries that repeatedly fail.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Confirmed defect is narrower: pendingCreditAcks clears all-or-nothi=
ng, so any credited-but-unacked payment is re-listed and re-internalized ev=
ery poll until an ack finally succeeds. The escalation to 'every later paym=
ent stranded forever' additionally requires the server to reject a batch co=
ntaining an unknown/expired id =E2=80=94 not established in this codebase a=
nd contrary to typical idempotent acknowledge behavior.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/rails/hand=
le.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"send-outbox-30day-beef-bloat-pr=
une-only-on-pay">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">30-day retention keeps the full AtomicBEEF for every sent payment; prune=
 runs only on the Pay screen</span><span class=3D"vtag v-partial">Partially=
 confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A user send=
s many PeerPay payments over weeks but rarely opens the Pay screen. Each se=
nt entry retains token.transaction (a full AtomicBEEF, often several KB). A=
ll entries live in one JSON blob under 'peerpay_outbox'. Every saveOutboxEn=
try (handle.ts sendViaHandle), every getOutboxEntries in WalletHomeScreen (=
516/564/764), every TaskDrainOutbox pass (WalletContext:1300), and every ha=
ndleResendRequests (228) reads and (for saves) rewrites the whole blob.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>pruneExpiredSent=
 is only ever called from HandleSend.loadOutbox (HandleSend.tsx:222). Nothi=
ng in the background monitor, WalletContext, or WalletHomeScreen prunes. So=
 sent entries =E2=80=94 each carrying the full BEEF =E2=80=94 accumulate an=
d are only trimmed when the user visits the Pay tab; if they never do, the =
blob grows without bound past 30 days. Every outbox read parses, and every =
save re-serializes, the entire multi-hundred-KB blob on the JS thread.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Unbounded KV growth =
and O(n) full-blob parse/serialize on the mobile JS thread on every send, e=
very home render that reads the outbox, and every ~5s TaskDrainOutbox tick =
when unsent rows exist. On a heavy sender this becomes a measurable UI stal=
l and storage bloat, with no upper bound if the Pay screen is not visited.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Run prune=
ExpiredSent from a background task (e.g. inside the TaskDrainOutbox lambda =
or a dedicated periodic task) rather than only on Pay-screen mount, and/or =
stop retaining the full token.transaction on sent entries (the BEEF is refe=
tchable by txid for resend). Also cap the number of retained sent entries.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>The accumulation is bounded, not unbounded: new outbox entries are =
only created via sendViaHandle on the Pay screen, whose mount/post-send loa=
dOutbox prunes. State the real risk as (a) retention exceedable when Pay is=
 never revisited and (b) O(N) whole-blob JSON parse/serialize of full-BEEF =
entries on the JS thread on every outbox read/write.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/outbox=
.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/HandleSend.t=
sx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletHomeScreen.tsx=
</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/context/WalletContext.tsx</c=
ode></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"send-overlay-outage-blocks-all-=
handle-sends">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">assertRecipientHostKnown blocks every handle send during an overlay outa=
ge with a misleading message</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirm=
ed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The ls_mess=
agebox overlay/LookupResolver is temporarily down or unreachable. queryAdve=
rtisements (MessageBoxClient) catches its own error and returns []; resolve=
HostForRecipient then falls back to this.host. In assertRecipientHostKnown =
(handle.ts:69-79) empty=3D=3D=3Dtrue and resolved=3D=3D=3Dclient.host, so i=
t throws RECIPIENT_HOST_UNKNOWN for EVERY recipient =E2=80=94 including rec=
ipients who have in fact advertised an inbox.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>An overlay failu=
re is indistinguishable here from 'recipient never anointed', and both are =
treated as a hard block before minting. HandleSend maps RECIPIENT_HOST_UNKN=
OWN to t('recipient_message_box_unknown') ('ask them to open the app once')=
, which is wrong guidance when the real cause is a transient overlay outage=
 on the sender's side.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>During any overlay o=
utage, all handle payments become un-sendable and the user is told the reci=
pient needs to open their app =E2=80=94 advice that will not fix anything. =
It is a self-inflicted send dead-end with misdirected copy, the sending-sid=
e analogue of the dead ends this work set out to remove.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Distingui=
sh an overlay lookup that failed/threw from one that returned an empty resu=
lt (e.g. have the client surface a lookup-error signal, or catch and classi=
fy). Only block on a definitive empty advertisement result; on lookup failu=
re, either proceed or surface a network-retry message rather than 'recipien=
t must open the app'.</p>

