<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"send-abandon-drops-valid-onchain-p=
ayment">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">Aba=
ndon after a persisted-late broadcast can tell the recipient to drop a vali=
d on-chain payment (fund loss window)</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed=
">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>In sendViaH=
andle the order is sendMessage -&gt; mark delivered -&gt; broadcastNoSend -=
&gt; markOutboxSent (handle.ts:491-501). If broadcastNoSend succeeds but ma=
rkOutboxSent does not persist (transient storage error / crash), the entry =
is delivered=3Dtrue, status=3D'unsent', and the tx is live on-chain. Before=
 TaskDrainOutbox self-heals it, the user taps Cancel; because delivered=3D=
=3D=3Dtrue the sheet offers Abandon; cancelOutboxPayment mode:'abandon' sen=
ds payment_cancelled (539-546). The recipient's consumePaymentCancelled the=
n drops the (still-uncredited) inbox token for a payment that is genuinely =
funded on-chain.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Abandon assumes =
a delivered-but-unsent entry means the transaction is not truly settled, bu=
t the markOutboxSent-failed-after-broadcast case breaks that assumption: th=
e money moved, yet the recipient is told to discard the token that carries =
the derivation data they need to spend it.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Narrow but real fund=
-loss: on-chain output locked to the recipient's address, recipient's token=
 deleted, sender's funds spent =E2=80=94 a dead end for both parties. Depen=
ds on a persistence failure between broadcast and markOutboxSent plus a use=
r Abandon before the drain retries.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Before ab=
andoning, confirm the backing tx is not already broadcast/known (e.g. listA=
ctions status check) and refuse to send payment_cancelled for a tx that has=
 left nosend; or make markOutboxSent + broadcast atomic/ordered so 'deliver=
ed &amp;&amp; unsent' can never coincide with a live broadcast.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/rails/hand=
le.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/HandleSend=
.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"send-resend-request-fallback-recip=
ient-leak">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">res=
end_request with no matching outbox entry rebuilds and sends the token to t=
he requester</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summa=
ry>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>An attacker=
 sends {type:'resend_request', txid:&lt;a txid the victim once paid&gt;} to=
 the victim's control box. If the victim's outbox entry for that txid has b=
een pruned (past 30 days) or is legacy, rebuildAndDeliver (handleResendRequ=
ests.ts:228-234) finds no entry; this app labels its sends only ['peerpay']=
 (no pubkey label), so recipientFromLabels returns undefined and recipient =
falls back to args.recipient =3D the control-message sender (the attacker).=
 The victim then refetches the BEEF and sends the rebuilt token to the atta=
cker, and acks the attacker's message.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The fallback rec=
ipient for a resend is the requester of the control message, with no check =
that the requester is the payment's original recipient. rebuildPeerPayToken=
 reuses the original locking script, so the attacker cannot spend the outpu=
t =E2=80=94 but the victim still performs a network refetch and delivers th=
e raw tx + derivation prefix/suffix to an arbitrary party on demand.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>No direct fund loss =
(output stays locked to the original recipient), but an unauthenticated thi=
rd party can trigger the victim's wallet to refetch a BEEF and hand over pa=
yment token data, and consumes the resend as 'answered'. Griefing and infor=
mation disclosure; only on the manual Home 'Resend' path (handleResendReque=
sts), not the automatic poll.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Do not fa=
ll back to the control-message sender as the delivery recipient. Deliver a =
rebuilt token only to a recipient established from the outbox entry (or a p=
ubkey label), and drop resend_requests whose txid maps to no known outbound=
 payment.</p>

