ResendRequests.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<h3 class=3D"group-title" id=3D"g-storage">Storage layer<span class=3D"grou=
p-count">11</span></h3>
<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"storage-reviewstatus-throws-on-co=
mpleted-tx">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">r=
eviewStatus rule 1 throws on a completed/proven tx, aborting and rolling ba=
ck the entire repair every run</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confi=
rmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A proven_tx=
_req sits at status 'invalid' while its transaction is 'completed' or has p=
rovenTxId set =E2=80=94 exactly the proof-outage-then-actually-mined state =
the refuted audit finding warned about (also reachable via backup-restore m=
erging rows of different ages, or the window between the patched TaskUnFail=
 resurrecting a tx and its req status being rewritten). TaskReviewStatus th=
en runs reviewStatus every 15 minutes.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>REVIEW_INVALID_R=
EQ_TXS_SQL (reviewStatusSql.ts:26-31) filters only `t.status &lt;&gt; 'fail=
ed'` =E2=80=94 no `t.provenTxId IS NULL` / `t.status &lt;&gt; 'completed'` =
guard. StorageExpoSQLite.ts:1676 then calls updateTransactionStatus('failed=
', ...) with no per-tx try/catch, and the inherited StorageProvider.updateT=
ransactionStatus throws WERR_INVALID_OPERATION for a completed or proven tx=
 (wallet-toolbox-mobile StorageProvider.js:414-420). The throw escapes the =
single transaction wrapping the whole of reviewStatus (StorageExpoSQLite.ts=
:1659), so every repair queued in that run =E2=80=94 including the input re=
stores of rules 2/3 =E2=80=94 rolls back, every run, until the poisoned row=
 is manually fixed. The codebase demonstrably knows about this throw: proce=
ssOfflineActions.ts:444-448 documents it and guards rejectOne with per-entr=
y try/catch; reviewStatus does not.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>The new reviewStatus=
 repair (commit f62bfe0, a headline audit fix) permanently self-disables on=
 the first occurrence: TaskReviewStatus errors every 15 minutes, and the Ch=
eck-my-wallet flow silently reports 0 repairs because WalletCheckScreen.tsx=
:166-168 swallows the throw =E2=80=94 the user is told their wallet was che=
cked while nothing was repaired. Stuck spendable/spentBy bookkeeping is nev=
er healed.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Add `AND =
t.provenTxId IS NULL AND t.status &lt;&gt; 'completed'` to REVIEW_INVALID_R=
EQ_TXS_SQL (both the constant and the test copy), and/or wrap the per-tx up=
dateTransactionStatus in try/catch that logs and continues, matching reject=
One in processOfflineActions.ts.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>One nit: upstream reviewStatusIdb has the same missing guard, but u=
pstream is not wrapped in a single transaction, so only this implementation=
 converts one poisoned row into a total, repeated rollback of all three rep=
air rules.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/storage/Storag=
eExpoSQLite.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/storage/method=
s/reviewStatusSql.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"storage-null-translation-only-s=
pentby">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">sqlUpdateValue NULL translation covers only outputs.spentBy; other clear=
-by-undefined upstream writes stay silent no-ops</span><span class=3D"vtag =
v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A user (or =
a BRC-100 app through the WebView interface) calls relinquishOutput, or int=
ernalizeAction re-internalizes an existing basket-insertion output as a wal=
let payment.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>sqlBindValue (sq=
lUpdateValue.ts:4-12) special-cases exactly one column. Upstream StoragePro=
vider.relinquishOutput passes `{ basketId: undefined }` intending to clear =
the basket (wallet-toolbox-mobile StorageProvider.js:568) =E2=80=94 omitted=
 by sqlBindValue, so the UPDATE has zero SET clauses (StorageExpoSQLite.ts:=
531 returns 0) and the output is never removed from its basket, while the w=
allet API still reports success. internalizeAction's mergeWalletPaymentForO=
utput likewise passes `customInstructions: undefined` to wipe stale customI=
nstructions when converting an output to change (internalizeAction.js:608-6=
20); the stale value survives =E2=80=94 notable because the new PeerPay tok=
en-rebuild path treats outputs.customInstructions as the source of truth fo=
r re-deriving payment keys. Additionally validatePartialForUpdate (StorageE=
xpoSQLite.ts:306-307) converts explicit null to undefined, so there is NO w=
ay for any caller to write NULL to any column other than outputs.spentBy.</=
p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>relinquishOutput is =
a functional no-op on this storage (pre-existing, but the same defect class=
 d75a3ec claims to fix); stale customInstructions on converted outputs can =
feed wrong derivation data into the new token-rebuild flow.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Extend th=
e translation to the known clear-by-undefined columns (outputs.basketId, ou=
tputs.customInstructions, outputs.senderIdentityKey, outputs.derivationPref=
ix/Suffix, outputs.spendingDescription) or, better, translate undefined=E2=
=86=92NULL for any key explicitly present in the update object while contin=
uing to omit absent keys =E2=80=94 Object.entries already distinguishes the=
 two.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Two corrections. (1) Mechanism: the UPDATE is not zero-clause =E2=
=80=94 validatePartialForUpdate always injects updated_at (StorageExpoSQLit=
e.ts:291), so the statement runs, touches only updated_at, and returns chan=
ges=3D1; the line-531 early return is rarely hit. The effect (clear silentl=
y dropped, success reported) is as claimed. (2) Scope: omitting undefined f=
or non-spentBy columns is pre-existing behavior (the old loop at the same s=
ite also skipped undefined) =E2=80=94 the in-range commit d75a3ec is an inc=
omplete fix, not a new regression.</p>
