<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"storage-reviewstatus-dbswap-con=
currency">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Long reviewStatus transaction plus the this.db-swap pattern exposes conc=
urrent direct-storage writes to silent rollback and connection scrambling</=
span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The user ru=
ns Check my wallet (WalletCheckScreen.tsx:161 calls storage.reviewStatus di=
rectly, bypassing WalletStorageManager's writer lock) while background Moni=
tor tasks or UI handlers (useOfflineNoticeActions.onDismiss via storage.sql=
iteDb, the SendWaiting patch's findOfflineActions) touch storage between re=
viewStatus's many awaits.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>StorageExpoSQLit=
e.transaction (lines 204-222) swaps this.db to the exclusive txn connection=
 for the whole scope; the sqliteDb getter (line 1725-1727) returns this.db,=
 so interleaved outside callers are handed the open transaction =E2=80=94 t=
heir writes join it and are rolled back if reviewStatus throws (which findi=
ng storage-reviewstatus-throws-on-completed-tx makes a live possibility). I=
f two transactions overlap (WalletCheck reviewStatus + TaskReviewStatus's o=
wn run, which use different locks), the nested swap/restore leaves this.db =
pointing at a finished txn connection after the outer restore. The pattern =
is pre-existing, but this range adds the first long, scan-heavy transaction=
 plus a second unserialized entry point, materially widening the window.</p=
>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Silently lost writes=
 (e.g. a dismissed rejection resurrects, an offline row's status update van=
ishes) or a wedge where subsequent storage calls hit a closed transaction c=
onnection until app restart.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Route Wal=
letCheckScreen's reviewStatus through the WalletStorageManager writer lock =
(runAsStorageProvider); longer term, replace the this.db swap with an expli=
cit connection parameter threaded via the TrxToken, or guard transaction() =
with an async mutex so two exclusive scopes cannot interleave.</p>

