eExpoSQLite.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletCh=
eckScreen.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"storage-reviewstatus-fails-mine=
d-tx-and-ignores-agedlimit">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">reviewStatus fails genuinely-mined unproven txs immediately and ignores =
agedLimit entirely</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span><=
/summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A proof out=
age marks a req 'invalid' (attempts exhausted) while the tx is actually min=
ed and still 'unproven'. TaskReviewStatus (15 min) runs before the patched =
TaskUnFail (10 min) next succeeds at getMerklePath.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The `agedLimit` =
argument (accepted at StorageExpoSQLite.ts:1658 and passed by TaskReviewSta=
tus as now-5min) is never read =E2=80=94 no aging or recent-activity guard =
delays failing a just-invalidated req. Because 'invalid' is in SAFE_REQ_STA=
TUSES (reviewStatusSql.ts:12), the tx is failed AND its inputs are restored=
 to spendable in the same pass; its real outputs (change) are marked unspen=
dable. This mirrors upstream reviewStatusIdb semantics, but the audit speci=
fically flagged that proof-outage 'invalid' reqs can be genuinely mined, an=
d the fix added only the offline-queue skip, not this guard.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>During an outage win=
dow the wallet offers coins that are already spent on chain: the next payme=
nt built from a restored input is a real double-spend that the network refu=
ses =E2=80=94 a fresh payment dead-end =E2=80=94 and received change disapp=
ears from the balance until the patched TaskUnFail happens to resurrect the=
 tx.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Honor age=
dLimit in REVIEW_INVALID_REQ_TXS_SQL (only act on reqs whose updated_at &lt=
; agedLimit), and consider requiring a failed getMerklePath re-check (or th=
e classifier's structural verdict) before restoring inputs whose failed spe=
nder was invalidated during a proof outage.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>The rescue framing is actually generous to the code: TaskUnFail (10=
 min) only processes reqs already set to 'unfail' (TaskUnFail.js:42) and no=
thing automatically moves 'invalid' to 'unfail' (TaskReviewDoubleSpends han=
dles only doubleSpend), so this is not a 15-vs-10-minute race =E2=80=94 an =
'invalid' req for a mined tx is failed permanently, with no automatic recov=
ery. Also note upstream reviewStatusIdb ignores agedLimit identically, so t=
his is inherited semantics rather than a local regression =E2=80=94 but rev=
iewStatus was a stub before this range, so the behavior is new to this wall=
et.</p>
