eExpoSQLite.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/storage/method=
s/reviewStatusSql.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"storage-reviewstatus-full-scans=
-in-exclusive-txn">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">reviewStatus full-scans outputs and all failed txs with N+1 req queries =
inside one exclusive write transaction, on unpurged tables</span><span clas=
s=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A mature wa=
llet: thousands of outputs and an ever-growing set of failed transactions (=
purgeData is still a stub at StorageExpoSQLite.ts:1711-1713, so nothing is =
ever purged). TaskReviewStatus runs every 15 minutes.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>REVIEW_OUTPUTS_S=
QL is `SELECT ... FROM outputs` with no WHERE (reviewStatusSql.ts:37) =E2=
=80=94 the whole table is loaded into JS each run; REVIEW_FAILED_TXS_SQL re=
turns every failed tx ever, then one REVIEW_REQ_STATUSES_SQL query per dist=
inct failed txid (StorageExpoSQLite.ts:1681-1688, classic N+1). All of it r=
uns inside withExclusiveTransactionAsync, which holds the write connection =
(and swaps this.db) for the full duration, blocking every other storage wri=
te, and the workload grows without bound because nothing purges failed hist=
ory.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Periodic multi-secon=
d write stalls on older wallets =E2=80=94 payments, internalize, and the of=
fline drain all queue behind the review; memory churn from materializing th=
e outputs table every 15 minutes.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Scope the=
 outputs query to relevant rows (`WHERE spentBy IN (...) OR transactionId I=
N (...)` built from the failed sets, or a JOIN against failed transactions)=
, batch the req-status lookups with one `txid IN (...)` query, and move the=
 read phase outside the write transaction (only the updates need it).</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Parity note: upstream reviewStatusIdb performs the same full output=
 scan and N+1 req reads, but not inside a single exclusive write transactio=
n =E2=80=94 the transaction wrapping and the resulting write-blocking windo=
w are local to this implementation.</p>
