<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"storage-sendwaiting-defer-reset=
s-drain-backoff">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">SendWaiting deferral kicks TaskSendOffline.requestNow() every pass, defe=
ating the drain's exponential backoff</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed=
">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A queued of=
fline parent stalls permanently (e.g. STALL_BAD_BEEF =E2=80=94 corrupt inpu=
tBEEF, refetch 404s because the parent was never broadcast) while a child r=
eq sits at 'unsent'. TaskSendWaiting runs every ~8 s while unsent reqs exis=
t.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>WalletContext.ts=
x:1375 calls TaskSendOffline.requestNow() whenever deferred &gt; 0, on ever=
y SendWaiting pass. requestNow (TaskSendOffline.ts:63-67) sets checkNow and=
 resets backoffMs/nextDueAt to zero, so the drain's documented 10s=E2=86=92=
5min exponential backoff ('the doubling keeps a genuinely stuck queue from =
spamming services', TaskSendOffline.ts:9-13) never engages. Each forced dra=
in pass re-runs findOfflineActions, per-row findReq, beef merges, and =E2=
=80=94 new in this range =E2=80=94 one uncached WhatsOnChain HTTP fetch per=
 unparseable/txid-only entry (processOfflineActions.ts:146,151-155; makeBee=
fRepair has no caching or backoff).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A single permanently=
