<details class=3D"finding sev-critical" open=3D"" id=3D"checkwallet-release=
-on-network-error-zeroes-balance">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-critical">critical</span><span class=3D"f=
title">Release pass marks every scanned output unspendable when WoC is unre=
achable or rate-limited</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</s=
pan></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>User is off=
line (or WoC is down / rate-limiting) and opens Check Wallet from Settings,=
 a failed-send prompt, NearbyFlow, or HandleReceive; the screen auto-runs o=
n mount. Or: a user restores from backup on a flaky connection and the post=
-restore validate pass runs.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>WalletCheckScree=
n.tsx:131-135 calls wallet.listOutputs({ basket: sdk.specOpInvalidChange, t=
ags: ['all','release'] }) and WalletContext.tsx:1094 calls wallet.reviewSpe=
ndableOutputs(false, true) after restore =E2=80=94 both with the 'release' =
tag and no online gate. In the toolbox, ListOutputsSpecOp.js filterOutputs =
does ok =3D await services.isUtxo(o) and adds the output to the release set=
 whenever ok =3D=3D=3D false. Services.isUtxo (Services.js:265-271) returns=
 `or.isUtxo =3D=3D=3D true`, and getUtxoStatus returns { status: 'error', i=
sUtxo: undefined } when every provider attempt fails (WhatsOnChain is the O=
NLY registered getUtxoStatus provider). So a network error, timeout, or sus=
tained 429 is indistinguishable from 'not a UTXO': every output whose isUtx=
o call fails is marked spendable =3D false via updateOutput. Offline, that =
is EVERY spendable output the query returns ('all' clears the basket filter=
, so all baskets). The screen's catch blocks never fire because nothing thr=
ows =E2=80=94 the pass 'succeeds' and the Done copy reports the destroyed o=
utputs as 'Freed N stuck coins'. Even online, INVALID_CHANGE_MAX_CONCURRENC=
Y=3D12 concurrent isUtxo calls against WoC's ~3 req/s free tier invites 429=
s; a 429 that survives the two 2s retries becomes an error result and a fal=
se release. No code path ever re-marks a still-unspent output spendable=3Dt=
rue (reviewStatus only restores outputs reserved by failed txs; checkUtxoSp=
endability only scans spendable=3Dtrue rows).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>One tap on Check Wal=
let while offline zeroes the wallet's visible spendable balance with no aut=
omatic recovery; the same can happen to a freshly restored wallet during im=
port. Funds are still on chain but the wallet can no longer construct spend=
s (insufficient funds), which for a non-technical user is a hard dead end =
=E2=80=94 the exact outcome this change set exists to prevent, produced by =
its own repair tool.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Gate both=
 call sites on getOnline() and, more fundamentally, never pass 'release' un=
less the isUtxo result was a definite success: run the spec-op WITHOUT 'rel=
ease' first, and only release outputs whose status was 'success' with isUtx=
o =3D=3D=3D false (requires distinguishing error from false =E2=80=94 e.g. =
call services.getUtxoStatus directly and check r.status, or patch filterOut=
puts usage with a wrapper). At minimum, skip the release pass entirely when=
 the first isUtxo call errors, and never run it from validateRestoredCoins =
without connectivity.</p>

