<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"checkwallet-all-errors-swallowed-=
reports-ok">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">E=
very port swallows all errors, so a check that did nothing reports 'Everyth=
ing looks good'</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></su=
mmary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Device offl=
ine, storage not ready, wallet still building, WoC down, or message box unr=
eachable =E2=80=94 user runs Check Wallet.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>All six ports in=
 useWalletCheckPorts (WalletCheckScreen.tsx:126-227) catch every error and =
return zero counts; the wallet=3D=3Dundefined and storage=3D=3Dnull guards =
do the same. checkUtxoSpendability itself returns strings like 'Wallet not =
ready' / 'Error querying outputs: =E2=80=A6' which parseCount silently conv=
erts to 0. Consequently runWalletCheck can never throw in production, the e=
rror branch and Retry button (WalletCheckScreen.tsx:325-336, wallet_check_f=
ailed) are effectively unreachable, and a run in which zero steps actually =
executed ends with haptics.success() and 'Everything looks good' (wallet_ch=
eck_ok). The stated requirement was that one step failing must not silently=
 abandon the rest =E2=80=94 the implementation overcorrects into all failur=
es masquerading as a clean bill of health, which for a repair-of-last-resor=
t screen is a lie at the worst moment.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A user whose wallet =
is genuinely broken runs the check while the network is flaky, is told ever=
ything is fine, and has no further recourse =E2=80=94 the dead end the flow=
 exists to remove. The Retry affordance the UI ships is dead code.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Have each=
 port return a third field (ok: boolean or error: string). runWalletCheck s=
hould aggregate per-step outcomes and the Done copy should distinguish 'che=
cked and fine' from 'couldn't check N steps =E2=80=94 try again when online=
'. Gate the auto-run on getOnline() and wallet/storage readiness, showing t=
he existing error+Retry UI otherwise.</p>

