<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"checkwallet-release-eats-queued-o=
ffline-change">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">R=
elease pass scans nosend outputs, so it releases the change of queued offli=
ne payments even on a healthy network</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed=
">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>User has an=
 offline payment queued (offline_actions status 'queued', tx status 'nosend=
' =E2=80=94 see core/offline/payerHold.ts, which explicitly keeps its chang=
e spendable so a second offline payment can chain off it), then runs Check =
Wallet while online because some other payment looked stuck.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>listOutputsSql.t=
s:86 feeds the specOpInvalidChange query txStatus ['completed','unproven','=
nosend'], so a queued offline payment's spendable change output is included=
 in the scan. A never-broadcast tx's output is by definition not a UTXO, so=
 WoC returns an empty result with status 'success' and isUtxo=3Dfalse (What=
sOnChain.js applyUtxoStatusResponse: data.result.length =3D=3D=3D 0 =E2=86=
=92 isUtxo=3Dfalse), and the 'release' tag marks it spendable=3Dfalse =E2=
=80=94 a false release requiring no network flakiness at all. Neither the t=
oolbox filterOutputs nor the app filters out txids with live queued/posting=
 offline_actions rows, violating the plan's own global guardrail (plan line=
 27: 'Skip txids with live offline_actions rows (queued/posting) in any pat=
h that would fail/release them') =E2=80=94 a guardrail the new reviewStatus=
Sql.ts does honor. The screen also widened the plan's spec ( Task 19: specO=
pInvalidChange with ['release'] ) to ['all','release'], extending the relea=
se surface from the default basket to every basket. There is also a smaller=
 race: a tx TaskSendOffline posted seconds ago ('unproven') may not yet be =
indexed by WoC, giving the same success/isUtxo=3Dfalse false release.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>The queued payment l=
ater posts fine, but its change output stays spendable=3Dfalse forever =E2=
=80=94 silent balance loss with no automatic repair path, caused by the rep=
air tool itself, in exactly the queued-offline scenario the audit demanded =
be protected.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Before re=
leasing, exclude outputs whose transaction has status 'nosend' (or whose tx=
id appears in offline_actions queued/posting =E2=80=94 same query reviewSta=
tusSql already uses), and drop the 'all' tag to match the plan. Alternative=
ly run the spec-op without 'release' and apply releases app-side after filt=
ering out queue-protected and nosend txids.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Two peripheral details: (a) after payerHold's promotion the queued =
payment's TRANSACTION is 'unproven', not 'nosend' ('nosend' only if the pro=
motion failed) =E2=80=94 both statuses are in the scanned list, so the defe=
ct is unchanged; (b) 'widened the plan's spec' is wrong: the design doc its=
elf specifies reviewSpendableOutputs(true, true) for the Check Wallet coins=
 step (2026-08-31-payment-dead-end-fixes-design.md:290), so ['all','release=
'] follows the spec =E2=80=94 only the restore path was spec'd as ['release=
'] (plan Task 19, line 1730).</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletCh=
eckScreen.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/storage/methods=
/listOutputsSql.ts</code><code>node_modules/@bsv/wallet-toolbox-mobile/out/=
src/storage/methods/ListOutputsSpecOp.js</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"checkwallet-no-reentrancy-or-ca=
ncellation">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">No reentrancy guard or cancellation: stacked pushes, Retry, and language=
 change can run several concurrent repair passes; leaving the screen does n=
ot stop one</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summar=
y>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>User taps t=
he Settings 'Check Wallet' row, backs out mid-run (Back always works, but t=
he run keeps going), taps the row again =E2=80=94 or a failed-send prompt p=
ushes /wallet-check while the Settings-launched run is still in its multi-m=
inute coins scan. Also: the run auto-restarts if `t` changes (useEffect key=
ed on run=E2=86=92[t]) e.g. on a language switch.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>WalletCheckScree=
n auto-runs on mount (useEffect at :275-277) and the only guard is per-inst=
ance component state; router.push stacks a new screen instance each time (W=
alletConfigScreen.tsx:838, HandleSend.tsx:281/326, AddressSend.tsx:134, Nea=
rbyFlow.tsx:2020, HandleReceive.tsx:325), so each push starts an independen=
t runWalletCheck with no module-level mutex (contrast creditInboxOnce, whic=
h has one). There is no AbortSignal: navigating away leaves the pass mutati=
ng storage (releaseStuck SQL, updateOutput spendable flips, internalizeActi=
on, 30-day sweep) with setState landing on an unmounted component. Two conc=
urrent passes double the WoC traffic (worsening the 429=E2=86=92false-relea=
se finding), can both decide to internalize the same spending tx / sweep th=
e same UTXO (mostly deduped by the toolbox merge path, but double-counted i=
n the summary), and interleave writes with the monitor's 5s task loop on th=
e same SQLite connection.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Duplicate multi-minu=
te network scans on a phone, inflated/incoherent Done summaries, higher odd=
s of rate-limit-driven false releases, and background mutation the user bel=
ieves they cancelled by leaving the screen.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Add a mod=
ule-level in-flight promise (same pattern as creditInboxOnce) so a second m=
ount joins the running pass and re-renders its progress; pass an aborted fl=
ag from unmount into runWalletCheck and check it between steps (and between=
 outputs in the coins scan).</p>

