<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"checkwallet-refresh-guard-gaps-=
sent-and-429">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">refreshProof guard protects queued/posting but leaves 'sent' rows and no=
n-404 HTTP failures able to fail a broadcast tx</span><span class=3D"vtag v=
-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>An offline =
payment was posted (offline_actions status 'sent', tx 'unproven', broadcast=
 &gt;5 minutes ago =E2=80=94 normal, blocks average ~10 minutes) and the us=
er taps Refresh while WoC returns 429/5xx on /tx/hash/{txid}.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>refreshProofGuar=
d.ts:20 only shields 'queued'/'posting'; the type deliberately models 'sent=
' (line 12) but shouldFailUnprovenTx treats it as fail-eligible. The remain=
ing protection is WalletContext.tsx:2244-2250's on-chain head check =E2=80=
=94 but `onChain =3D head.ok` treats ANY non-2xx (429 rate limit, 5xx, WoC =
maintenance page) as 'not on chain', after which an unproven tx older than =
5 minutes is marked failed at :2277, releasing inputs the payee's mempool t=
x already spends =E2=80=94 the double-spend the guard exists to prevent. Th=
e head-check pattern is pre-existing, but the new guard explicitly enumerat=
ed 'sent' and chose not to protect it, and the new WalletCheck/badge flows =
encourage exactly this Refresh-while-degraded behavior.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A rate-limited Refre=
sh on a healthy 6-minute-old payment can fail it locally and free its input=
s for re-spending =E2=80=94 fund-safety relevant, though it needs a 429/5xx=
 (not a clean 404) plus a &gt;5-minute-old unproven tx.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Treat onl=
y head.status =3D=3D=3D 404 as evidence of absence (return 'pending' for an=
y other non-ok status), and extend shouldFailUnprovenTx to return 'pending'=
 for offlineStatus =3D=3D=3D 'sent' until the outbox row is acknowledged or=
 rejected.</p>

