<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"checkwallet-sqlite-txn-connecti=
on-swap-race">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Check-pass writes can interleave with a monitor task's exclusive transac=
tion via the this.db connection swap</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed"=
>Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The wallet =
check's records step runs storage.reviewStatus (wrapped in this.transaction=
) at the same moment a monitor task (TaskCreditInbox internalize, TaskSendO=
ffline drain =E2=80=94 all on a ~5s cadence) or another check step issues s=
torage reads/writes.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>StorageExpoSQLit=
e.transaction (StorageExpoSQLite.ts:193-222) temporarily replaces this.db w=
ith the exclusive-transaction connection for the whole scope. Any concurren=
t async caller that goes through getDB()/sqliteDb during that window (check=
UtxoSpendability's updateOutput, releaseStuckReservations' raw runAsync, mo=
nitor task writes) silently executes INSIDE the other caller's transaction:=
 its writes commit or roll back with a transaction it knows nothing about, =
and a nested this.transaction call during the window invokes withExclusiveT=
ransactionAsync on the txn object (nested-transaction error). The swap patt=
ern is pre-existing, but this range is what created real concurrency agains=
t it: reviewStatus was a stub returning '' before (old WalletContext had no=
 transactional review), and the new auto-running check plus TaskCreditInbox=
/TaskDrainOutbox multiply simultaneous writers.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Lost or phantom-roll=
ed-back repair writes (an output release that vanishes, or an unrelated wri=
te dragged down by a failed reviewStatus), and intermittent 'cannot start a=
 transaction within a transaction' errors that the check's catch-all conver=
ts into a false 'Everything looks good'.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Serialize=
 storage access with an async mutex around this.transaction and route all w=
rites through it, or stop swapping this.db and instead pass the txn connect=
ion explicitly through the TrxToken so concurrent callers keep using the ma=
in connection's queue.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>One sub-mechanism is wrong in detail: a nested this.transaction cal=
l during the window does not produce a nested-transaction error. expo-sqlit=
e's Transaction extends SQLiteDatabase (node_modules/expo-sqlite/src/SQLite=
Database.ts:787-796), so withExclusiveTransactionAsync on the swapped objec=
t opens ANOTHER new connection via Transaction.createAsync =E2=80=94 the fa=
ilure manifests as lock contention ('database is locked'/SQLITE_BUSY, or a =
stall until the outer commits), not a clean nested-BEGIN error. The silent-=
interleaving hazard for plain reads/writes stands as claimed.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/storage/Storag=
eExpoSQLite.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletCh=
eckScreen.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"checkwallet-unbounded-runtime-n=
o-cap-or-warning">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Coins and sweep steps are unbounded and unthrottled where it matters: mi=
nutes-long runs with a frozen '2 of 4' bar and no cap, no cancel, no durati=
on warning</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary=
>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Wallet with=
 a few hundred spendable outputs runs Check Wallet; or any wallet runs it o=
n a slow connection.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The coins step d=
oes the network scan twice: first the spec-op isUtxo pass (one WoC script-h=
ash call per output, concurrency 12, up to 2 retries with 2s waits each =E2=
=80=94 on failure ~4-8s per output), then checkUtxoSpendability's per-outpu=
t /spent poll at WalletContext.tsx:2360-2368 (throttled to 340ms, 10s timeo=
ut, plus a BEEF fetch per spent output). 500 outputs =E2=89=88 3+ minutes f=
or the /spent pass alone, on top of the spec-op pass. sweepAddresses (Walle=
tCheckScreen.tsx:206-226) then fires 30 sequential UNTHROTTLED WoC address =
lookups (getUtxosForAddress at address.ts:114-120 has no throttle, no timeo=
ut, and rp.result.filter throws on a 429 body =E2=80=94 the day is then sil=
ently skipped). The UI shows only 'N of 4' with a step label; there is no i=
ntra-step progress, no output cap, no elapsed-time hint, and no cancel cont=
rol, so the bar sits at 2 of 4 for minutes and reads as hung. The 12-concur=
rent spec-op burst plus the 30-call sweep also actively provoke WoC's ~3 re=
q/s limit, feeding both the false-release finding and silent sweep misses (=
'Looking for missed payments=E2=80=A6' that actually skipped most days).</p=
>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Non-technical users =
will assume the app froze and kill it mid-repair; rate-limit fallout silent=
ly degrades the very checks being reported as complete.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Share one=
 throttle across all WoC traffic in the check (including the sweep and the =
spec-op pass), cap the coins scan (e.g. newest N outputs with a 'ran a part=
ial check' note), surface per-step counts ('checked 120 of 480 coins'), and=
 honor a cancellation flag between outputs.</p>

