<h3 class=3D"group-title" id=3D"g-headers">Headers, reorgs &amp; proofs<spa=
n class=3D"group-count">7</span></h3>
<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"headers-stale-extra-root-shadows-=
canonical-window">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">E=
xtra-root cache is never invalidated on rewind and now shadows the validate=
d window, poisoning a reorged height permanently</span><span class=3D"vtag =
v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The local h=
eader window only syncs at wallet build and on online transitions (never fr=
om TaskNewHeader), so during any online session fresh payments confirm at h=
eights ABOVE the local tip. Each such verification calls OfflineFirstChaint=
racks.isValidRootForHeight -&gt; putExtraRoot(height, remoteRoot) (OfflineF=
irstChaintracks.ts:90), and the new inReorgWindow guard (headerStore.ts:304=
-307) does NOT block above-tip heights (height &gt; tipHeight fails the fir=
st condition), so the most reorg-prone heights are exactly the ones cached =
into &lt;chain&gt;-extra.json. Now block at height H is orphaned. The next =
sync rewinds (truncateToCount, headerStore.ts:213-234) and appends the cano=
nical header at H =E2=80=94 but neither truncateToCount nor reset() (header=
Store.ts:296-302, which deliberately keeps extra) removes extra[H].</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>rootForHeight wa=
s flipped in this range to prefer extra over the window (headerStore.ts:146=
-156: 'A heal written to extra is the value to consult'), so the stale orph=
aned root permanently shadows the freshly-validated canonical header. The t=
hree heal paths are all blocked: (1) prewarmOwnRoots skips any height rootF=
orHeight already answers (prewarm.ts:30), so it can never overwrite a stale=
 extra; (2) the online heal putExtraRoot at OfflineFirstChaintracks.ts:90 i=
s silently skipped by the inReorgWindow guard (headerStore.ts:237) exactly =
during the post-reorg window when the heal is needed =E2=80=94 the code sti=
ll logs 'healed' (OfflineFirstChaintracks.ts:91-95) even though nothing was=
 written; (3) nothing else ever deletes extra entries. The new test '__test=
s__/headers/headerStore.test.ts prefers an extra root over the window' bake=
s the shadowing in as intended behavior.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>For the poisoned hei=
ght, offline verification gives wrong answers forever: a BEEF proving inclu=
sion in the ORPHANED block passes the local=3D=3D=3Droot fast path (Offline=
FirstChaintracks.ts:59-60) and is accepted offline =E2=80=94 the wallet cre=
dits a proof for a tx that may be double-spent on the canonical chain (fund=
-loss adjacent); conversely every canonical BEEF at that height is refused =
offline (payment dead-end of exactly the class this fix set was meant to el=
iminate). Online it self-heals per call only once the height is more than 6=
 below the local tip AND some verification for that height happens again.</=
p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>On trunca=
teToCount/reset, delete extra entries for all heights &gt;=3D the new tip -=
 6 (or for the truncated range); make append() drop extra[h] for every heig=
ht it writes into the window (the window header is validated PoW, strictly =
better evidence than a cached network answer); and let putExtraRoot overwri=
te an EXISTING extra entry even inside the reorg window (the guard should o=
nly block creating new entries). Alternatively revert the precedence flip a=
nd give heals a dedicated overwrite path into the window index.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>One word overstates: 'permanently'. Once the local tip advances mor=
e than 6 past the height (needs a later sync) AND some online verification =
re-asks that exact height, putExtraRoot does overwrite the stale entry (the=
 extra[key] =3D=3D=3D root short-circuit fails on the differing value and i=
nReorgWindow is then false). But nothing schedules or guarantees such a re-=
verification =E2=80=94 healing is opportunistic =E2=80=94 so 'persists inde=
finitely in practice, with no guaranteed heal' is the precise statement.</p=
>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/headers/header=
Store.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/headers/OfflineFirst=
Chaintracks.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/headers/prewar=
m.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"headers-miss-slot-snapshot-clas=
sifies-wrong-pass">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Credit classifier consumes lastMissHeight BEFORE the pass runs, so a hea=
ders-behind failure is classified structural on its first occurrence and bu=
rns an auto-attempt</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span>=
</summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Device is o=
nline but its header window/chaintracks can't resolve the root for an incom=
ing payment's height (window behind, service behind tip). TaskCreditInbox b=
uilds the classifier via makeCreditClassifier (WalletContext.tsx:1277-1281;=
 HandleReceive.tsx:494-497), which calls takeLastMissHeight() ONCE, BEFORE =
creditInboxOnce runs. The internalize then fails with 'The tx parameter mus=
t be valid AtomicBEEF' and only NOW records lastMissHeight (OfflineFirstCha=
intracks.ts:73/84/112).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>classifyCreditEr=
ror sees lastMissHeight=3Dundefined and offline=3Dfalse, the AtomicBEEF mes=
sage matches neither the network regex nor double-spend, so the failure is =
classified 'structural' (creditErrors.ts:16-23) and counted against MAX_AUT=
O_ATTEMPTS=3D2 (handle.ts:298-307). The miss recorded during pass N is only=
 visible to pass N+1's snapshot =E2=80=94 the mechanism is systematically o=
ne pass late. The reverse contamination also holds: lastMissHeight is a sin=
gle consume-once slot on the tracker that successes never clear and that th=
ree independent consumers share (TaskCreditInbox, HandleReceive's 5s focuse=
d poll, WalletCheckScreen:190) =E2=80=94 a stale miss left by any unrelated=
 verification (refreshProof, reproveProven, a tx-detail view) makes the NEX=
T pass classify a genuinely corrupt payment as 'environmental', so it is ne=
ver counted, never NACKed, and is re-internalized on every pass; with a bel=
ow-window payment sitting in the same box re-arming the slot each pass, the=
 corrupt payment loops indefinitely and the sender is never told.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Half the auto-retry =
budget is wrongly burned on the exact environmental condition (headers behi=
nd) the classification was built to protect =E2=80=94 'environmental failur=
es must not burn the 2 auto-attempts' is only met from the second pass onwa=
rd; and cross-contamination can indefinitely suppress the NACK-before-disca=
rd path for structural failures, recreating a silent dead end.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Classify =
per failure, not per pass: have accept()'s catch read takeLastMissHeight() =
immediately after the failed internalize (pass a per-payment context into c=
lassify), or record the miss keyed by height/txid instead of a single globa=
l slot; clear the slot on successful verification of the same height.</p>

