rs.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/headers/OfflineFirstCha=
intracks.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/context/WalletCon=
text.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/HandleR=
eceive.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"headers-reviewproventxs-cadence=
-and-cost">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Re-enabled ReviewProvenTxs runs every 1 minute forever (2 chaintracks HT=
TP calls/pass), does a 100-request burst on empty wallets, and spins with a=
n error DB write per minute when offline and behind</span><span class=3D"vt=
ag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Any wallet =
after this range (the task was previously spliced out on mobile; WalletCont=
ext.tsx:1417-1420 now keeps it). (a) Steady state: TaskReviewProvenTxs.trig=
gerNextMsecs starts at triggerQuickMsecs=3D1min (TaskReviewProvenTxs.js:28)=
 and the caught-up path returns early on range.isEmpty (js:45-46) WITHOUT e=
ver setting the 10-minute cadence (that reset lives in reviewHeightRange's =
own isEmpty branch, js:71-73, which the early return makes unreachable) =E2=
=80=94 so the task runs every minute forever, each run doing chaintracks.cu=
rrentHeight() (HTTP) in runTask PLUS a second currentHeight() (HTTP) added =
by the patched getLastReviewedHeight (walletMonitor.ts:123-135) plus 1-2 SQ=
L queries. (b) Fresh wallet with ZERO proven_txs: getLastReviewedHeight ret=
urns undefined, the patch jumps to tip-199 and the first run performs 100 s=
equential remote findHeaderForHeight HTTP calls and 100 findProvenTxs-by-he=
ight SQL queries against an empty table. (c) Device goes offline while the =
review span is non-empty (e.g. airplane mode shortly after build): findHead=
erForHeight always delegates to the remote (OfflineFirstChaintracks.ts:141-=
143), the fetch throws out of reviewHeightRange, Monitor.runOnce logs an 'e=
rror1' row into monitor_events =E2=80=94 repeated every 60s for as long as =
the device is offline. TaskPurge sits in _otherTasks (Monitor.js:152) which=
 the scheduler never runs, so monitor_events (which also gains one JSON row=
 per non-empty review) grows without bound.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>boundReviewProve=
nTxs fixed the genesis crawl but inherited the library's cadence bug and ad=
ded a second per-pass network call, added no proven_txs-emptiness guard, an=
d no offline gate =E2=80=94 three costs that did not exist when the task wa=
s removed at dfa97d0. (The 100-height passes themselves are network-bound a=
waits, not synchronous CPU, so no JS-thread freeze =E2=80=94 the 5s monitor=
 loop concern does not apply here.)</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Battery/data drain (=
3x the intended chaintracks polling, forever), a pointless 100-request burs=
t on every fresh install/restore, and unbounded monitor_events growth on of=
fline devices.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>In boundR=
eviewProvenTxs: after a caught-up pass set task.triggerNextMsecs =3D task.t=
riggerMsecs (mirror the configureNewHeaderPolling fix); skip the pass entir=
ely when getOnline() is false or when the wallet has no proven_txs in the c=
andidate range (one COUNT query); reuse runTask's tip instead of a second c=
urrentHeight(); and schedule TaskPurge (or purge monitor_events directly) s=
o review/error rows are bounded.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>One mechanism detail is moot rather than wrong: TaskPurge sitting i=
n _otherTasks (Monitor.js:152) is not why monitor_events grows =E2=80=94 Ta=
skPurge calls purgeData (TaskPurge.js:28), which is a no-op returning {coun=
t:0} in this app's StorageExpoSQLite (StorageExpoSQLite.ts:1711-1713), and =
the library's purge does not cover monitor_events anyway (no purge path ref=
erences that table). The unbounded-growth conclusion holds a fortiori: noth=
ing at all prunes monitor_events.</p>
