<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"headers-rewind-full-file-rewrit=
e-per-step">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">Each single-header rewind reads and synchronously rewrites the entire ~4=
.6MB header bin; REWIND_CAP=3D144 allows ~660MB of blocking I/O plus 144 re=
fetches on a server anomaly</span><span class=3D"vtag v-unverified">Not re-=
verified</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A mainnet w=
indow is ~57k headers (~4.6MB, checkpoint 907,324 to present, growing ~4MB/=
yr with no rotation). A 2-block reorg: syncHeaders rewinds one header per l=
oop iteration (syncHeaders.ts:62-65), and every truncateToCount call reads =
the whole .bin and rewrites all of it minus 80 bytes (headerStore.ts:222-22=
9). expo-file-system's File.write is a synchronous JSI call (fs.ts:59-64; i=
OS Data.write / Android FileOutputStream), so each step blocks the JS threa=
d for a multi-MB write; the torn-bin heal on open (headerStore.ts:130-133) =
does the same full synchronous write during wallet build. Worse: the rewind=
 path triggers on a string-matched 'previous hash' error for the chunk's FI=
RST header (syncHeaders.ts:29-32) with no confirmation from the remote that=
 the local tip is actually orphaned =E2=80=94 a chaintracks node serving mi=
saligned/stale chunks during a deep catch-up makes the loop rewind up to 14=
4 GOOD headers, costing up to 144 x (4.6MB read + 4.6MB sync write) plus up=
 to 144 refetched 2000-header chunks (~46MB), then reset() discards the who=
le window and the next sync re-downloads a year of headers.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>truncateToCount =
is O(window) in disk I/O per single dropped header, called in a loop of up =
to 144; the reorg inference never validates against the remote (e.g. compar=
ing findHeaderForHeight(tipHeight).hash to store.tipHash) before destroying=
 local state.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>UI jank/freeze durin=
g reorgs (multi-hundred-ms per step on the JS thread, several steps per reo=
rg); pathological data/battery/disk churn and full-window loss when the hea=
der source misbehaves =E2=80=94 the exact mobile-thread cost profile this a=
udit flags. Normal 1-2 block reorgs are merely janky, not incorrect.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Confirm t=
he reorg first (one findHeaderForHeight at the local tip; only rewind if th=
e hash differs), walk back to the fork point in memory using single-header =
probes, then truncate ONCE to the fork height; or track a logical count in =
meta and truncate lazily (open() already heals a too-long bin, so deferring=
 the physical shrink to the next open is safe). Cap practical rewind depth =
well below 144 before resetting.</p>

