Store.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/headers/syncHeaders.=
ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/headers/fs.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"headers-taskreorg-wiring-is-ine=
rt-in-production">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">TaskReorg 'wiring' never receives events: ChaintracksServiceClient.subsc=
ribeReorgs is unimplemented, so live reorg repair does not exist and the on=
ly repair path lags ~100 blocks</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Conf=
irmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Every produ=
ction wallet build: createWalletMonitor (walletMonitor.ts:63-73) awaits mon=
itor.ready; Monitor._init calls offlineChaintracks.subscribeReorgs which de=
legates (OfflineFirstChaintracks.ts:165-167) to ChaintracksServiceClient, w=
hose subscribeReorgs/subscribeHeaders unconditionally throw 'Method not imp=
lemented.' (node_modules/@bsv/wallet-toolbox-mobile/out/src/services/chaint=
racker/chaintracks/ChaintracksServiceClient.js:24-29).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>monitor.deactiva=
tedHeaders is only populated by the subscription callback, so TaskReorg.tri=
gger never returns run=3Dtrue =E2=80=94 the 'TaskReorg subscribe' half of t=
he audit fix is dead code on every build (the code itself admits it in the =
walletMonitor.ts:59-61 comment, but the commit message and task list claim =
TaskReorg is wired). The actual reorg repair is TaskReviewProvenTxs with mi=
nBlockAge=3D100: maxEligibleHeight =3D tip-100 (TaskReviewProvenTxs.js:40),=
 so a proven_tx invalidated by a reorg is not audited until its height is ~=
100 blocks (~17 hours) deep. Until then getBeef/exports serve the stale pro=
of and offline re-verification of that coin's ancestry can fail. Positive s=
ide verified: awaiting monitor.ready adds NO startup latency or offline han=
g, because the client rejects without network I/O and createWalletMonitor c=
atches it; monitor.destroy() (which would re-await the rejected promise and=
 throw) is never called by WalletContext.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>The claimed live-reo=
rg coverage does not exist; reorg-corrupted proofs persist for ~17h with no=
 faster automatic path (refreshProof is manual). If a future chaintracksWit=
hEvents implements a real (network) subscribe, awaiting monitor.ready would=
 then block wallet build on a network call =E2=80=94 worth a timeout now.</=
p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Either im=
plement/deploy an events-capable chaintracks client (SSE) so subscribeReorg=
s works, or drop the inert wiring and instead drive reorg repair from the l=
ocal header store: syncHeaders already detects the orphan at rewind time =
=E2=80=94 call storage.reproveHeader(orphanedTipHash) for each truncated he=
ader, which repairs proven_txs within minutes instead of 17 hours. Wrap the=
 monitor.ready await in a timeout for forward-safety.</p>

