<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"headers-refreshproof-blockhash-not=
-crosschecked">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">ref=
reshProof stores a blockHash that is never checked to be the block containi=
ng the BUMP's merkle root</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed<=
/span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>refreshProo=
f validates the WoC BUMP's root via ct.isValidRootForHeight (WalletContext.=
tsx:2206) =E2=80=94 which can succeed on the LOCAL fast path against a stal=
e extra root (see the extra-shadow finding) or against the local window whi=
le the remote has since reorged =E2=80=94 then separately fetches the block=
Hash from ct.findHeaderForHeight (WalletContext.tsx:2212-2218) without comp=
aring header.merkleRoot to the BUMP's computed root.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Two independent =
sources (WoC for the proof, chaintracks/local store for the hash) are combi=
ned without a consistency check, so a reorg race or a poisoned extra entry =
produces a proven_tx row whose blockHash names a block that does not contai=
n the tx and whose merkleRoot does not match that block.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Internally inconsist=
ent proven_txs row; BEEFs exported with that proof reference the wrong bloc=
k; downstream reproveHeader lookups by blockHash match the wrong record. Se=
lf-corrects only ~17h later via the ReviewProvenTxs root comparison. Narrow=
 window, but the whole point of this commit (5cf29f3) was to stop persistin=
g untrustworthy proof fields.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>After fin=
dHeaderForHeight, require rootHex(header.merkleRoot) =3D=3D=3D merkleRoot b=
efore persisting (and when using store.tipHash, require the window root at =
that height to equal the BUMP root, bypassing the extra cache); return 'pen=
ding' on mismatch.</p>

