<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"headers-test-gaps-rewind-cap-and-e=
xtra-staleness">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">No =
tests for the rewind cap/reset path, deeper-than-one reorgs, or extra-root =
staleness across a rewind</span><span class=3D"vtag v-partial">Partially co=
nfirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The only re=
wind test covers a 1-deep reorg on a 1-header store (which actually exercis=
es truncateToCount(0)=3Dreset, not the truncate path through fs.writeBytes =
with a remaining prefix). Nothing tests: a 2+ deep rewind, the REWIND_CAP e=
xhaustion -&gt; reset() -&gt; rethrow path, a crash-torn bin SHORTER than m=
eta (full-reset direction), or that an extra root written above the tip sti=
ll shadows the window after the window later covers that height with a diff=
erent root (the dangerous case; the existing 'prefers extra' test only cove=
rs the same-root-irrelevant case).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The highest-risk=
 new code paths (cap boundary, multi-step truncate + tipHash recompute acro=
ss steps, reset-keeps-extra interaction) ship untested; the multi-step trun=
cate is exactly where an off-by-one in keep/subarray or a stale currentTipH=
ash would hide.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Regressions in rewin=
d arithmetic or the reset path would not be caught; the extra-shadow bug (f=
inding 1) is effectively test-enshrined.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Add tests=
: 3-deep reorg over a 5-header store asserting tipHash equals blockHash of =
the fork header after each step; rewind cap reached -&gt; store reset (coun=
t 0, tip =3D anchor) and error rethrown; open() with bin shorter than meta =
-&gt; reset; extra root at height H + later canonical window covering H -&g=
t; assert which root is served (currently documents the bug).</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Restate as: multi-step (2+ deep) rewinds, the REWIND_CAP=E2=86=92re=
set=E2=86=92rethrow path, and the bin-shorter-than-meta reset (pre-existing=
 code) ship untested; single-step truncate with a remaining prefix and the =
different-root extra-shadowing scenario ARE tested (headerStore.test.ts:178=
-188 and 207-212 respectively), the latter asserting the defective behavior=
 as intended rather than leaving it uncovered.</p>
