<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"ui-control-channel-unauthenticate=
d-consumers">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">p=
ayment_cancelled and resend_request are acted on without verifying the cont=
rol-message sender</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span><=
/summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Anyone can =
send messages to any box. (a) An attacker who learns the txid of a delivere=
d-but-not-yet-credited payment sends {type:'payment_cancelled', txid} to th=
e recipient's payment_control box. (b) An attacker sends {type:'resend_requ=
est', txid} for a victim's peerpay payment older than the 30-day outbox ret=
ention.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>(a) consumePayme=
ntCancelled =E2=86=92 dropInboxTokenForTxid (handleResendRequests.ts:67-92)=
 acknowledges (deletes) every un-credited payment_inbox token whose transac=
tion matches the txid, without ever comparing msg.sender to the token's sen=
der =E2=80=94 destroying the recipient's only copy of the derivation data. =
It runs automatically from the home screen's focus poll and HandleSend's mo=
unt poll. (b) rebuildAndDeliver's recipient fallback (line 232-233) is `arg=
s.recipient` =3D the control-message sender; sendViaHandle only labels acti=
ons ['peerpay'] (handle.ts:446), so recipientFromLabels finds nothing for a=
ny action, and once the outbox entry is pruned (30 days) the rebuilt token =
=E2=80=94 full BEEF + derivation prefix/suffix + amount =E2=80=94 is delive=
red TO THE REQUESTER when the user taps the home-screen Resend row.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>(a) is a fund-loss v=
ector: a token deleted before credit leaves on-chain money the recipient ca=
n no longer derive keys for (recovery only via the sender's manual 'Send de=
tails again' while their outbox copy survives). (b) leaks payment metadata =
to an arbitrary third party via a one-tap social-engineered 'Resend request=
ed' row that shows no requester identity. Exploitability is bounded by need=
ing the txid, but a malicious or buggy counterparty always has it.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>For payme=
nt_cancelled: only drop inbox tokens whose message sender equals the contro=
l message's sender. For resend_request: never fall back to delivering to th=
e requester =E2=80=94 require the recorded recipient (outbox entry or a rec=
ipient label written at send time; add the recipient pubkey as an action la=
bel in sendViaHandle), and show the requester's identity on the Resend row.=
</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Severity nuance on (b): the leaked token's output is locked to a ke=
y derived toward the ORIGINAL recipient, so the requester most likely canno=
t spend the funds =E2=80=94 it is derivation-data/amount/BEEF disclosure pl=
us misdelivery (the real recipient never gets the resend and the request is=
 acked as satisfied), not direct theft. (a) is the fund-loss-grade issue.</=
p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/handle=
ResendRequests.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/con=
trol.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/rails/handle.ts</=
code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletHomeScreen.tsx</co=
de></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"ui-pending-corrupt-dead-end-and-q=
uarantine-growth">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">C=
orrupt localpay pending blob is never repaired: receives permanently broken=
, quarantine copies written on every poll</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confi=
rmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>PENDING_KEY=
 JSON becomes corrupt once (crash mid-write, disk issue). The user then ope=
ns the home screen or /pay, or receives a new nearby payment.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>readAll (pending=
.ts:81-90) copies the corrupt blob to a NEW key `localpay_pending_corrupt_$=
{Date.now()}` and throws =E2=80=94 but PENDING_KEY itself is never reset or=
 repaired by anything (no code writes PENDING_KEY after a quarantine). Cons=
equences: (1) every subsequent readAll re-quarantines ANOTHER full copy =E2=
=80=94 readUnprocessedPending is now called on every txStatusVersion bump b=
y both WalletHomeScreen.fetchOfflineRows (line 474) and PayScreen's queue e=
ffect (line 221), so the key_value store grows by blob-size per bump, unbou=
ndedly; (2) savePending throws forever (pending.ts:110-117), so the payee c=
an never accept another nearby payment =E2=80=94 settleReceived fails with =
the raw English string 'pending queue JSON is corrupt' and a Retry that can=
 never succeed (NearbyFlow.tsx:806-817); (3) the pendingCorrupt card in Off=
lineNotice (lines 214-221) is title-only =E2=80=94 no button, no repair pat=
h =E2=80=94 and WalletCheck has no step for it.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Permanent payee-side=
 payment dead end (the exact failure class this audit set out to eliminate)=
 plus unbounded storage growth on a mobile device, with no corrective actio=
n offered to either party.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>On quaran=
tine: copy the blob aside ONCE (fixed key or dedupe by content hash), then =
reset PENDING_KEY to the salvageable subset (parse entry-by-entry) or []. G=
ive the pendingCorrupt notice an action (e.g. 'Repair' that performs exactl=
y that), or add it as a WalletCheck step.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/localpay/pendi=
ng.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletHomeScreen.=
tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/PayScreen.tsx</code=
><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/OfflineNotice.tsx</co=
de></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-high" id=3D"ui-pending-queue-unbounded-growth=
-and-retry">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-high">high</span><span class=3D"ftitle">l=
ocalpay_pending never prunes completed entries and re-internalizes failed o=
nes forever; whole blob JSON-parsed on the JS thread per home-screen bump</=
span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A user rece=
ives nearby payments over weeks; one arriving frame is structurally bad (in=
ternalizeAction always throws).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Nothing ever rem=
oves entries from PENDING_KEY: savePending appends, updateStatus maps, and =
no prune exists =E2=80=94 every entry keeps its full AtomicBEEF as a JSON n=
umber array (can be tens-to-hundreds of KB each). getUnprocessed/readUnproc=
essedPending parses and re-materializes the WHOLE blob (fromWire Uint8Array=
 copies) on the JS thread, and the new code calls it on every txStatusVersi=
on bump on both the home screen (WalletHomeScreen.tsx:474) and PayScreen (l=
ine 221) =E2=80=94 i.e. every ~5s while the monitor is writing. Separately,=
 getUnprocessed includes 'failed' entries (pending.ts:128-130) and processP=
ending has no attempt ceiling, so a permanently-bad frame is re-internalize=
d (BEEF validation + SQL) on every wallet build, every reconnect, and every=
 nearby settle (WalletContext.tsx:1866-1915, NearbyFlow.tsx:863), each pass=
 costing two full-queue rewrites; its pendingCount badge shows '1 waiting' =
forever with no user action to clear it.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Progressive JS-threa=
d jank on the two most-used screens (parse cost grows with lifetime receive=
 count), storage bloat, wasted wallet writes every monitor pass, and a perm=
anently-stuck 'waiting to internalize' count that is itself a dead end.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Prune com=
pleted entries (and cap failed ones with an attempts counter mirroring MAX_=
AUTO_ATTEMPTS) inside processPending's writebacks; cache readUnprocessedPen=
ding or store a count key separately so the badge does not require parsing =
every transaction ever received.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>One softening: readUnprocessedPending runs per txStatusVersion bump=
, not literally every 5s =E2=80=94 the monitor bumps the version only when =
statuses actually change. The unbounded-growth and forever-retry mechanics =
are exactly as claimed.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/localpay/pendi=
ng.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletHomeScreen.=
tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/PayScreen.tsx</code=
><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/context/WalletContext.tsx</code></=
div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"ui-background-credit-swallows-a=
