<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"ui-classifier-miss-height-race"=
>
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">takeLastMissHeight is consumed by classifiers whose pass never runs, bur=
ning auto-attempts on environmental failures</span><span class=3D"vtag v-co=
nfirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Headers are=
 behind; a credit pass fails and the chain tracker records lastMissHeight. =
HandleReceive's 5s poll and TaskCreditInbox both build classifiers (each ca=
lling the take-once takeLastMissHeight) before calling creditInboxOnce; one=
 of them joins the other's in-flight pass.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>makeCreditClassi=
fier consumes takeLastMissHeight at build time (creditErrors.ts:33-40), but=
 creditInboxOnce discards a joiner's args entirely (creditInbox.ts:193 `if =
(inFlight &amp;&amp; force.length =3D=3D=3D 0) return inFlight`). The joine=
r's consumed miss-height is lost, so the pass that actually runs classifies=
 header-miss failures ('valid AtomicBEEF') as structural, incrementing atte=
mpts. Idle 5s polls also consume the signal with no failure to classify. Tw=
o structural counts =E2=86=92 give-up =E2=86=92 resend_request NACK sent to=
 the sender for a payment that only needed headers to catch up.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>The environmental-vs=
-structural mechanism this fix-set added can be defeated by its own two con=
sumers racing: retries are burned on network conditions and the sender is a=
sked to resend unnecessarily.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Move clas=
sifier construction inside runCreditInbox (consume the miss-height once per=
 pass that actually runs), or make lastMissHeight peek-with-TTL instead of =
take-once.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/H=
andleReceive.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/context/Wall=
etContext.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/creditInbox=
.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/creditErrors.ts</code=
></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"ui-nearby-kill-on-exit-sheet-st=
rands-nosend">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">App killed on the send_qr screen or its exit-question sheet strands the =
noSend build with no re-showable code</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed=
">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Payer build=
s a QR payment (send_qr showing, or the 'did they scan?' ChoiceSheet up via=
 Cancel/back), then the app is killed or crashes before Done/no is chosen.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>Nothing is persi=
sted until Done ('yes'/'unsure') runs finalizeDelivery's hold, or 'no' runs=
 abortBuild (NearbyFlow.tsx:1300-1368). On kill, the noSend action keeps am=
ount+fee locked, there is no queue row and no framePayload, so the sealed Q=
R can never be re-shown (the payee's PSK-bound session is also gone). The o=
nly recovery is spotting a 'nosend' row in the activity list and tapping it=
s Abort chip (ActivityRow ABORTABLE_STATUSES includes 'nosend') =E2=80=94 w=
hich is unsafe if the payee DID scan before the kill, since freeing the inp=
uts invites a conflict with the payee's later broadcast, and nothing warns =
about that.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Funds locked invisib=
ly (amount+fee at nosend) after a crash at the exact decision point the new=
 exit-question flow created; the manual recovery both requires expertise an=
d can double-spend the payee.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Persist a=
n 'unresolved QR handover' marker (reference, txid, sealed framePayload, se=
ssionless) the moment send_qr is entered; on next launch re-ask the did-the=
y-scan question from that marker, routing to the same hold/abort outcomes.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Minor: the parenthetical 'the payee's PSK-bound session is also gon=
e' is only true if the payee's screen also reset; the payer-side loss of th=
e sealed bytes alone already makes the code unrecoverable.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/N=
earbyFlow.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"ui-received-overlay-refire-on-a=
ck-failure">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">HandleReceive full-screen ReceivedOverlay re-fires and re-counts amounts=
 every poll while inbox acks fail</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Co=
nfirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>internalize=
Action succeeds but acknowledgeMessage fails (acknowledgeCredited swallows =
it, handle.ts:185-192) =E2=80=94 e.g. the box accepts list reads but its ac=
k endpoint errors intermittently.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The credited pay=
ment stays listed with no attempts entry, so the next 5s pass re-accepts it=
 (internalizeAction is an idempotent merge by txid and returns accepted) =
=E2=86=92 outcome.accepted &gt; 0 again =E2=86=92 applyCreditResult raises =
the ReceivedOverlay again with sound (HandleReceive.tsx:476-487, PaymentSuc=
cessOverlay tone on mount), after the user already dismissed it. The summed=
 amount also re-counts every still-listed already-credited payment, so the =
figure can overstate what just arrived.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Repeated full-screen=
 'you got paid' moments (with audio) for money received once, and a wrong a=
mount on the receipt =E2=80=94 a trust-destroying UX bug on the money-arriv=
al path.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Track cre=
dited-but-unacked message ids (pendingCreditAcks is already module-state =
=E2=80=94 expose it) and exclude them from both the accepted count and the =
overlay sum; or make accept() report 'already credited' distinctly from a f=
resh credit.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Confidence caveat: the refire depends on the toolbox's internalizeA=
ction returning success on a repeat merge =E2=80=94 asserted by this repo's=
 own comments and relied on elsewhere (session-spent replay), but I did not=
 re-verify the toolbox source.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/H=
andleReceive.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/pay/rails/ha=
ndle.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-medium" id=3D"ui-resend-request-permanent-ban=
ner-dos">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-medium">medium</span><span class=3D"ftitl=
e">An unanswerable resend_request is never acked and never dismissable =E2=
=80=94 permanent home-screen banner, attacker-triggerable</span><span class=
=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>Anyone send=
s {type:'resend_request', txid:'garbage', reason:'uncreditible'} to a user'=
s payment_control box (or a legit request references a payment the wallet g=
enuinely cannot rebuild).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>listPendingResen=
dRequests stores it as unanswered (handleResendRequests.ts:194-201) and the=
 home screen renders the 'Resend requested' row (WalletHomeScreen.tsx:976-9=
99). Tapping Resend runs handleResendRequests, whose rebuild fails (no outb=
ox entry, no matching action) =E2=86=92 the row goes to `pending`, the cont=
rol message is NEVER acked (ack only happens on successful delivery, line 2=
88), and the user sees showToast(t('unknown_error')) (WalletHomeScreen.tsx:=
715). There is no dismiss affordance and no ack-on-unresolvable path, so th=
e banner re-lists on every focus forever.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A permanent, un-dism=
issable warning row plus a misleading 'unknown error' toast on the exact co=
rrective control this audit added =E2=80=94 a new dead end that any peer (o=
r attacker) can pin to the victim's home screen with one message.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Ack (or l=
ocally suppress with a dismissed-set) resend_requests whose txid matches no=
 outbox entry and no peerpay action after N attempts; add a dismiss action =
to the row; replace the unknown_error toast with copy naming the txid that =
could not be rebuilt.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/peerpay/handle=
ResendRequests.ts</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/Walle=
tHomeScreen.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"ui-handlesend-stale-outbox-blocks-=
send">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">Han=
dleSend's send button stays blocked on a stale outbox after the background =
drain succeeds</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></sum=
mary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A send fail=
s on delivery (unsent outbox entry). The user leaves the screen open; TaskD=
rainOutbox later delivers and broadcasts it in the background.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>canSend requires=
 outbox.length =3D=3D=3D 0 (HandleSend.tsx:423-424) but loadOutbox runs onl=
y on mount and after the screen's own actions; nothing re-loads when TaskDr=
ainOutbox drains the entry, so the stale row keeps the CTA disabled and the=
 'finish or cancel' hint showing until the user leaves and re-enters the ce=
ll.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>A user is blocked fr=
om paying by a warning about a payment that already completed =E2=80=94 a m=
inor but real dead-end impression on the primary send path.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Re-run lo=
adOutbox on txStatusVersion bumps or on a focus effect, or have TaskDrainOu=
tbox bump a version the screen subscribes to.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/H=
andleSend.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"ui-pending-aborts-kept-forever">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">rep=
layPendingAborts retries permanently-failing references on every wallet bui=
ld; queue never shrinks and RMW can drop entries</span><span class=3D"vtag =
v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>A queued ab=
ort's reference no longer exists (action already sent, or storage was resto=
red from backup) so abortAction throws on every replay; separately, two fai=
led aborts are queued concurrently (finalizeDelivery decline path and abort=
Build).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>replayPendingAbo=
rts keeps any entry whose abortAction throws (pendingAborts.ts:57-64) with =
no attempt counter or terminal-error classification, so it is retried on ev=
ery wallet build forever. queuePendingAbort is a read-modify-write on one k=
ey with no lock (lines 40-45) =E2=80=94 concurrent queues (NearbyFlow.tsx:1=
113, 1251, 1327 call sites) can lose an entry, silently orphaning a stuck U=
TXO.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Bounded-per-run but =
unbounded-over-time retry list (wasted work each build); in the race case a=
 stuck-UTXO release is silently dropped, leaving funds locked with no retry=
.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Drop entr=
ies whose abortAction throws a definitive invalid-reference error (keep onl=
y transient failures), add an attempts cap, and serialize queuePendingAbort=
 through a module promise chain like pending.ts's withQueueLock.</p>
<p class=3D"fld corr"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Verifier=E2=80=99s correctio=
n</span>Scope note: the replay runs once per wallet build, not on a timer, =
so the retry cost is bounded per session; the growth is a never-shrinking l=
ist plus one failed wallet call per entry per build. The RMW-loss window is=
 real but narrow =E2=80=94 it needs two aborts to fail and interleave.</p>
<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/core/localpay/pendi=
ngAborts.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"ui-poll-identity-and-beef-parse-ch=
urn">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">Han=
dleReceive re-resolves sender identities over the network and re-parses Ato=
micBEEFs on every 5s poll</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed<=
/span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The Get Pai=
d screen is open with one or more attention rows.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>fetchPayments ca=
lls resolveIdentity (an uncached overlay network lookup, possibly plus a UH=
RP hop) for every distinct sender on every 5-second tick (HandleReceive.tsx=
:524-528), and each AttentionRow render re-runs satoshisFromToken =E2=86=92=
 Transaction.fromAtomicBEEF over the full token bytes (line 264) because ev=
ery poll replaces payments/attempts state identities. saveInboxAttempts als=
o rewrites its KV key every pass even when unchanged (creditInbox.ts:164).<=
/p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Steady network chatt=
er and JS-thread parse work proportional to attention-row count while the s=
creen is up =E2=80=94 battery and jank cost on exactly the screen a user wa=
tches while waiting to be paid.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Cache res=
olved identities by key (they are presentation-only), memoize satoshisFromT=
oken per messageId, and skip saveInboxAttempts when the map is deep-equal t=
o the prior one.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/components/pay/H=
andleReceive.tsx</code><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/resolveIdentit=
y.ts</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low" id=3D"ui-resend-partial-failure-unknown-=
error">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">Hom=
e 'Resend' shows the generic unknown_error toast whenever any request remai=
ns pending</span><span class=3D"vtag v-confirmed">Confirmed</span></summary=
>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>The user ta=
ps Resend on the home banner; some tokens rebuild and deliver, one cannot (=
offline BEEF refetch failed, or a bogus request).</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>onResendPending =
treats r.pending.length &gt; 0 as `showToast(t('unknown_error'))` (WalletHo=
meScreen.tsx:713-715) even when resent &gt; 0 =E2=80=94 no distinction betw=
een partial success, a retryable network failure, and an unanswerable reque=
st.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>The corrective actio=
n this fix-set added reports 'unknown error' on its most common partial out=
come, teaching users the repair button is broken.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Toast a s=
pecific message using r.resent and r.pending.length (e.g. 'Resent 2, 1 stil=
l pending'), and only use error styling when resent =3D=3D=3D 0.</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletHo=
meScreen.tsx</code></div>
</div></details>
<details class=3D"finding sev-low refuted" id=3D"ui-walletconfig-hardcoded-=
color">
<summary><span class=3D"chip chip-low">low</span><span class=3D"ftitle">Che=
ck Wallet settings row uses a hard-coded #0A84FF instead of a theme token</=
span><span class=3D"vtag v-refuted">Refuted</span></summary>
<div class=3D"fbody">
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">When it happens</span>User opens =
Settings in light or dark theme.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">The defect</span>The new Check Wa=
llet ListRow passes iconColor=3D"#0A84FF" (WalletConfigScreen.tsx:~833) whi=
le every other row in the file uses theme tokens.</p>
<p class=3D"fld"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Impact</span>Cosmetic inconsisten=
cy; may clash with custom themes.</p>
<p class=3D"fld fix"><span class=3D"fldlabel">Suggested fix</span>Use color=
s.info (or whatever token the neighboring rows use).</p>

<div class=3D"files"><code>packages/expo-wallet-toolbox/ui/screens/WalletCo=
nfigScreen.tsx</code></div>
